Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"g2-2-42":{"route":"#/gitav/2.42","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:42:en2","title":"Gita 2.42, in another translation","body":"O Pârtha, no set determination is formed in the minds of those that are deeply attached to pleasure and power, and whose discrimination is stolen away by the flowery words of the unwise, who are full of desires and look upon heaven as their highest goal and who, taking pleasure in the panegyric words of the Vedas, declare that there is nothing else.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","42 of 72"]]},"gv-2-43":{"route":"#/gitav/2.43","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:43:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.43","text":"कामात्मानः स्वर्गपरा जन्मकर्मफलप्रदाम् ।\nक्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं प्रति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kāmātmānaḥ svargaparā janmakarmaphalapradām |\nkriyāviśeṣabahulāṃ bhogaiśvaryagatiṃ prati ||","body":"With desire for self, with heaven for goal, they offer birth as the fruit of action, and prescribe many and various ceremonies for the attainment of pleasure and lordship.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","43 of 72"]]},"gv-2-44":{"route":"#/gitav/2.44","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:44:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.44","text":"भोगैश्वर्यप्रसक्तानां तयापहृतचेतसाम् ।\nव्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न विधीयते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"bhogaiśvaryaprasaktānāṃ tayāpahṛtacetasām |\nvyavasāyātmikā buddhiḥ samādhau na vidhīyate ||","body":"For them who cling to pleasure and lordship, whose minds are captivated by such teaching, is not designed this determinate Reason, on contemplation steadily bent.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","44 of 72"]]},"gv-2-45":{"route":"#/gitav/2.45","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:45:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.45","text":"त्रैगुण्यविषया वेदा निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो नित्यसत्त्वस्थो निर्योगक्षेम आत्मवान् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"traiguṇyaviṣayā vedā nistraiguṇyo bhavārjuna |\nnirdvandvo nityasattvastho niryogakṣema ātmavān ||","body":"The Vedas deal with the three attributes; be thou above these three attributes, O Arjuna; beyond the pairs of opposites, ever steadfast in purity, careless of possessions, full of the Self.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","45 of 72"]]},"g2-2-45":{"route":"#/gitav/2.45","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:45:en2","title":"Gita 2.45, in another translation","body":"The Vedas deal with the three Gunas. Be thou free, O Arjuna, from the triad of the Gunas, free from the pairs of opposites, ever-balanced, free from (the thought of) getting and keeping, and established in the Self.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","45 of 72"]]},"gv-2-46":{"route":"#/gitav/2.46","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:46:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.46","text":"यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके ।\nतावान्सर्वेषु वेदेषु ब्राह्मणस्य विजानतः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yāvānartha udapāne sarvataḥ saṃplutodake |\ntāvānsarveṣu vedeṣu brāhmaṇasya vijānataḥ ||","body":"All the Vedas are as useful to an enlightened Brâhmana as is a tank in a place covered all over with water.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","46 of 72"]]},"g2-2-46":{"route":"#/gitav/2.46","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:46:en2","title":"Gita 2.46, in another translation","body":"To the Brâhmana who has known the Self, all the Vedas are of so much use as a reservoir is, when there is a flood everywhere.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","46 of 72"]]},"gv-2-47":{"route":"#/gitav/2.47","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:47:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.47","text":"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmaṇyevādhikāraste mā phaleṣu kadācana |\nmā karmaphalaheturbhūrmā te saṅgo’stvakarmaṇi ||","body":"Thy business is with the action only, never with its fruits; so let not the fruit of action be thy motive, nor be thou to inaction attached.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","47 of 72"]]},"g2-2-47":{"route":"#/gitav/2.47","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:47:en2","title":"Gita 2.47, in another translation","body":"Thy right is to work only; but never to the fruits thereof. Be thou not the producer of the fruits of (thy) actions; neither let thy attachment be towards inaction.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","47 of 72"]]},"gv-2-48":{"route":"#/gitav/2.48","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:48:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.48","text":"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yogasthaḥ kuru karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā dhanañjaya |\nsiddhyasiddhyoḥ samo bhūtvā samatvaṃ yoga ucyate ||","body":"Perform action, O Dhananjaya, dwelling in union with the divine, renouncing attachments and balanced evenly in success and failure: equilibrium is called yoga.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","48 of 72"]]},"g2-2-48":{"route":"#/gitav/2.48","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:48:en2","title":"Gita 2.48, in another translation","body":"Being steadfast in Yoga, Dhananjaya, perform actions, abandoning attachment, remaining unconcerned as regards success and failure. This evenness. of mind (in regard to success and failure) is known as Yoga.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","48 of 72"]]},"gv-2-49":{"route":"#/gitav/2.49","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:49:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.49","text":"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय ।\nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"dūreṇa hyavaraṃ karma buddhiyogāddhanañjaya |\nbuddhau śaraṇamanviccha kṛpaṇāḥ phalahetavaḥ ||","body":"Far lower than the Yoga of Discrimination is action, O Dhananjaya. Take thou refuge in the Pure Reason; pitiable are they who work for fruit.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","49 of 72"]]},"g2-2-49":{"route":"#/gitav/2.49","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:49:en2","title":"Gita 2.49, in another translation","body":"Work (with desire) is verily far inferior to that performed with the mind undisturbed by thoughts of results. O [paragraph continues] Dhananjaya, seek refuge in this evenness of mind. Wretched are they who act for results.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","49 of 72"]]},"gv-2-50":{"route":"#/gitav/2.50","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:50:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.50","text":"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते ।\nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"buddhiyukto jahātīha ubhe sukṛtaduṣkṛte |\ntasmādyogāya yujyasva yogaḥ karmasu kauśalam ||","body":"United to the Pure Reason one abandoneth here both good and evil deeds; therefore cleave thou to yoga; yoga is skill in action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","50 of 72"]]},"g2-2-50":{"route":"#/gitav/2.50","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:50:en2","title":"Gita 2.50, in another translation","body":"Endued with this evenness of mind, one frees oneself in this life, alike from vice and virtue. Devote thyself, therefore, to this Yoga. Yoga is the very dexterity of work.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","50 of 72"]]},"gv-2-51":{"route":"#/gitav/2.51","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:51:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.51","text":"कर्मजं बुद्धियुक्ता हि फलं त्यक्त्वा मनीषिणः ।\nजन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmajaṃ buddhiyuktā hi phalaṃ tyaktvā manīṣiṇaḥ |\njanmabandhavinirmuktāḥ padaṃ gacchantyanāmayam ||","body":"The Sages, united to the Pure Reason, renounce the fruit which action yieldeth, and, liberated from the bonds of birth, they go to the blissful seat.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","51 of 72"]]},"g2-2-51":{"route":"#/gitav/2.51","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:51:en2","title":"Gita 2.51, in another translation","body":"The wise, possessed of this evenness of mind, abandoning the fruits of their actions, freed for ever from the fetters of birth, go to that state which is beyond all evil.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","51 of 72"]]},"gv-2-52":{"route":"#/gitav/2.52","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:52:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.52","text":"यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति ।\nतदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य श्रुतस्य च ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadā te mohakalilaṃ buddhirvyatitariṣyati |\ntadā gantāsi nirvedaṃ śrotavyasya śrutasya ca ||","body":"When thy mind shall escape from this tangle of delusion, then thou shalt rise to indifference as to what has been heard and shall be heard.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","52 of 72"]]},"g2-2-52":{"route":"#/gitav/2.52","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:52:en2","title":"Gita 2.52, in another translation","body":"When thy intellect crosses beyond the taint of illusion, then shalt thou attain to indifference, regarding things heard and things yet to be heard.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","52 of 72"]]},"gv-2-53":{"route":"#/gitav/2.53","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:53:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.53","text":"श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला ।\nसमाधावचला बुद्धिस्तदा योगमवाप्स्यसि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śrutivipratipannā te yadā sthāsyati niścalā |\nsamādhāvacalā buddhistadā yogamavāpsyasi ||","body":"When thy mind, bewildered by the Scriptures, shall stand immovable, fixed in contemplation, then shalt thou attain unto yoga.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","53 of 72"]]},"g2-2-53":{"route":"#/gitav/2.53","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:53:en2","title":"Gita 2.53, in another translation","body":"When thy intellect, tossed about by the conflict of opinions—has become immovable and firmly established in the Self, then thou shalt attain Self-realisation.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","53 of 72"]]},"gv-2-54":{"route":"#/gitav/2.54","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:54:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.54","text":"स्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा समाधिस्थस्य केशव ।\nस्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत किमासीत व्रजेत किम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sthitaprajñasya kā bhāṣā samādhisthasya keśava |\nsthitadhīḥ kiṃ prabhāṣeta kimāsīta vrajeta kim ||","body":"Arjuna said: What the mark, of him who is stable of mind, steadfast in contemplation, O Keshava? How doth the stable-minded talk, how doth he sit, how walk?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","54 of 72"]]},"g2-2-54":{"route":"#/gitav/2.54","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:54:en2","title":"Gita 2.54, in another translation","body":"What, O Keshava, is the description of the man of steady wisdom, merged in Samâdhi? How (on the other hand) does the man of steady wisdom speak, how sit, how walk?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","54 of 72"]]},"gv-2-55":{"route":"#/gitav/2.55","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:55:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.55","text":"प्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान् पार्थ मनोगतान् ।\nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"prajahāti yadā kāmān sarvān pārtha manogatān |\nātmanyevātmanā tuṣṭaḥ sthitaprajñastadocyate ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: When a man abandoneth, O Pârtha, all the desires of the heart, and is satisfied in the Self by the Self, then is he called stable in mind.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","55 of 72"]]},"g2-2-55":{"route":"#/gitav/2.55","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:55:en2","title":"Gita 2.55, in another translation","body":"When a man completely casts away, O Pârtha, all the desires of the mind, satisfied in the Self alone by the Self, then is he said to be one of steady wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","55 of 72"]]},"gv-2-56":{"route":"#/gitav/2.56","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:56:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.56","text":"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः ।\nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"duḥkheṣvanudvignamanāḥ sukheṣu vigataspṛhaḥ |\nvītarāgabhayakrodhaḥ sthitadhīrmunirucyate ||","body":"He whose mind is free from anxiety amid pains, indifferent amid pleasures, loosed from passion, fear and anger, is called a sage of stable mind.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","56 of 72"]]},"g2-2-56":{"route":"#/gitav/2.56","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:56:en2","title":"Gita 2.56, in another translation","body":"He whose mind is not shaken by adversity, who does not hanker after happiness, who has become free from affection, fear, and wrath, is indeed the Muni of steady wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","56 of 72"]]},"gv-2-57":{"route":"#/gitav/2.57","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:57:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.57","text":"यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहस्तत्तत्प्राप्य शुभाशुभम् ।\nनाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yaḥ sarvatrānabhisnehastattatprāpya śubhāśubham |\nnābhinandati na dveṣṭi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","body":"He who on every side is without attachments, whatever hap of fair and foul, who neither likes nor dislikes, of such a one the understanding is well poised.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","57 of 72"]]},"g2-2-57":{"route":"#/gitav/2.57","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:57:en2","title":"Gita 2.57, in another translation","body":"He who is everywhere unattached, not pleased at receiving good, nor vexed at evil, his wisdom is fixed.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","57 of 72"]]},"gv-2-58":{"route":"#/gitav/2.58","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:58:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.58","text":"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadā saṃharate cāyaṃ kūrmo’ṅgānīva sarvaśaḥ |\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","body":"When, again, as a tortoise draws in on all sides its limbs, he withdraws his senses from the objects of sense, then is his understanding well poised.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","58 of 72"]]},"g2-2-58":{"route":"#/gitav/2.58","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:58:en2","title":"Gita 2.58, in another translation","body":"When also, like the tortoise its limbs, he can completely withdraw the senses from their objects, then his wisdom becomes steady.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","58 of 72"]]},"gv-2-59":{"route":"#/gitav/2.59","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:59:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.59","text":"विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः ।\nरसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"viṣayā vinivartante nirāhārasya dehinaḥ |\nrasavarjaṃ raso’pyasya paraṃ dṛṣṭvā nivartate ||","body":"The objects of sense, but not the relish for them, turn away from an abstemious dweller in the body; and even relish turneth away from him after the Supreme is seen.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","59 of 72"]]},"g2-2-59":{"route":"#/gitav/2.59","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:59:en2","title":"Gita 2.59, in another translation","body":"Objects fall away from the abstinent man, leaving the longing behind. But his longing also ceases, who sees the Supreme.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","59 of 72"]]},"gv-2-60":{"route":"#/gitav/2.60","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:60:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.60","text":"यततो ह्यपि कौन्तेय पुरुषस्य विपश्चितः ।\nइन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yatato hyapi kaunteya puruṣasya vipaścitaḥ |\nindriyāṇi pramāthīni haranti prasabhaṃ manaḥ ||","body":"O son of Kuntî, the excited senses of even a wise man, though he be striving, impetuously carry away his mind.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","60 of 72"]]},"g2-2-60":{"route":"#/gitav/2.60","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:60:en2","title":"Gita 2.60, in another translation","body":"The turbulent senses, O son of Kunti, do violently snatch away the mind of even a wise man, striving after perfection.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","60 of 72"]]},"gv-2-61":{"route":"#/gitav/2.61","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:61:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.61","text":"तानि सर्वाणि संयम्य युक्त आसीत मत्परः ।\nवशे हि यस्येन्द्रियाणि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tāni sarvāṇi saṃyamya yukta āsīta matparaḥ |\nvaśe hi yasyendriyāṇi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","body":"Having restrained them all, he should sit harmonised, I his supreme goal; for, whose senses are mastered, of him the understanding is well poised.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","61 of 72"]]},"g2-2-61":{"route":"#/gitav/2.61","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:61:en2","title":"Gita 2.61, in another translation","body":"The steadfast, having controlled them all, sits focussed on Me as the Supreme. His wisdom is steady, whose senses are under control.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","61 of 72"]]},"gv-2-62":{"route":"#/gitav/2.62","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:62:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.62","text":"ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते ।\nसङ्गात् संजायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"dhyāyato viṣayānpuṃsaḥ saṅgasteṣūpajāyate |\nsaṅgāt saṃjāyate kāmaḥ kāmātkrodho’bhijāyate ||","body":"Man, musing on the objects of sense, conceiveth an attachment to these; from attachment ariseth desire; from desire anger cometh forth;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","62 of 72"]]},"g2-2-62":{"route":"#/gitav/2.62","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:62:en2","title":"Gita 2.62, in another translation","body":"Thinking of objects, attachment to them is formed in a man. From attachment longing, and from longing anger grows.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","62 of 72"]]},"gv-2-63":{"route":"#/gitav/2.63","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:63:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.63","text":"क्रोधाद्भवति संमोहः संमोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः ।\nस्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"krodhādbhavati saṃmohaḥ saṃmohātsmṛtivibhramaḥ |\nsmṛtibhraṃśād buddhināśo buddhināśātpraṇaśyati ||","body":"From anger proceedeth delusion; from delusion confused memory; from confused memory the destruction of Reason; from destruction of Reason he perishes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","63 of 72"]]},"g2-2-63":{"route":"#/gitav/2.63","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:63:en2","title":"Gita 2.63, in another translation","body":"From anger comes delusion, and from delusion loss of memory. From loss of memory comes the ruin of discrimination, and from the ruin of discrimination he perishes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","63 of 72"]]},"gv-2-64":{"route":"#/gitav/2.64","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:64:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.64","text":"रागद्वेषवियुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन् ।\nआत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"rāgadveṣaviyuktaistu viṣayānindriyaiścaran |\nātmavaśyairvidheyātmā prasādamadhigacchati ||","body":"But the disciplined self, moving among sense-objects with senses free from attraction and repulsion, mastered by the Self, goeth to peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","64 of 72"]]},"g2-2-64":{"route":"#/gitav/2.64","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:64:en2","title":"Gita 2.64, in another translation","body":"But the self-controlled man, moving among objects with senses under restraint, and free from attraction and aversion, attains to tranquillity.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","64 of 72"]]},"gv-2-65":{"route":"#/gitav/2.65","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:65:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.65","text":"प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते ।\nप्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"prasāde sarvaduḥkhānāṃ hānirasyopajāyate |\nprasannacetaso hyāśu buddhiḥ paryavatiṣṭhate ||","body":"In that Peace the extinction of all pains ariseth for him, for of him whose heart is peaceful the Reason soon attaineth equilibrium.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","65 of 72"]]},"g2-2-65":{"route":"#/gitav/2.65","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:65:en2","title":"Gita 2.65, in another translation","body":"In tranquillity, all sorrow is destroyed. For the intellect of him who is tranquil-minded, is soon established in firmness.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","65 of 72"]]},"gv-2-66":{"route":"#/gitav/2.66","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:66:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.66","text":"नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना ।\nन चाभावयतः शान्तिरशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"nāsti buddhirayuktasya na cāyuktasya bhāvanā |\nna cābhāvayataḥ śāntiraśāntasya kutaḥ sukham ||","body":"There is no Pure Reason for the non-harmonised, nor for the non-harmonised is there concentration; for him without concentration there is no peace, and for the unpeaceful how can there be happiness?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","66 of 72"]]},"g2-2-66":{"route":"#/gitav/2.66","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:66:en2","title":"Gita 2.66, in another translation","body":"No knowledge (of the Self) has the unsteady. Nor has he meditation. To the unmeditative there is no peace. And how can one without peace have happiness?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","66 of 72"]]},"gv-2-67":{"route":"#/gitav/2.67","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:67:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.67","text":"इन्द्रियाणां हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते ।\nतदस्य हरति प्रज्ञां वायुर्नावमिवाम्भसि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"indriyāṇāṃ hi caratāṃ yanmano’nuvidhīyate |\ntadasya harati prajñāṃ vāyurnāvamivāmbhasi ||","body":"Such of the roving senses as the mind yieldeth to, that hurries away the understanding, just as the gale hurries away a ship upon the waters.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","67 of 72"]]},"g2-2-67":{"route":"#/gitav/2.67","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:67:en2","title":"Gita 2.67, in another translation","body":"For, the mind which follows in the wake of the wandering senses, carries away his discrimination, as a wind (carries away from its course) a boat on the waters.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","67 of 72"]]},"gv-2-68":{"route":"#/gitav/2.68","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:68:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.68","text":"तस्माद्यस्य महाबाहो निगृहीतानि सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tasmādyasya mahābāho nigṛhītāni sarvaśaḥ |\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","body":"Therefore, O mighty-armed, whose senses are all completely restrained from the objects of sense, of him the understanding is well poised.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","68 of 72"]]},"g2-2-68":{"route":"#/gitav/2.68","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:68:en2","title":"Gita 2.68, in another translation","body":"Therefore, O mighty-armed, his knowledge is steady, whose senses are completely restrained from their objects.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","68 of 72"]]},"gv-2-69":{"route":"#/gitav/2.69","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:69:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.69","text":"या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी ।\nयस्यां जाग्रति भूतानि सा निशा पश्यतो मुनेः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yā niśā sarvabhūtānāṃ tasyāṃ jāgarti saṃyamī |\nyasyāṃ jāgrati bhūtāni sā niśā paśyato muneḥ ||","body":"That which is the night of all beings, for the disciplined man is the time of waking; when other beings are waking, then is it night for the sage who seeth.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","69 of 72"]]},"g2-2-69":{"route":"#/gitav/2.69","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:69:en2","title":"Gita 2.69, in another translation","body":"That which is night to all beings, in that the self-controlled man wakes. That in which all beings wake, is night to the Self-seeing Muni.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","69 of 72"]]},"gv-2-70":{"route":"#/gitav/2.70","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:70:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.70","text":"आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं ।\nसमुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत् ।\nतद्वत्कामा यं प्रविशन्ति सर्वे ।\nस शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"āpūryamāṇamacalapratiṣṭhaṃ |\nsamudramāpaḥ praviśanti yadvat |\ntadvatkāmā yaṃ praviśanti sarve |\nsa śāntimāpnoti na kāmakāmī ||","body":"He attaineth Peace, into whom all desires flow as rivers flow into the ocean, which is filled with water, but remaineth unmoved—not he who desireth desires.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","70 of 72"]]},"g2-2-70":{"route":"#/gitav/2.70","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:70:en2","title":"Gita 2.70, in another translation","body":"As into the ocean,—brimful, and still,—flow the waters, even so the Muni into whom enter all desires, he, and not the desirer of desires, attains to peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","70 of 72"]]},"gv-2-71":{"route":"#/gitav/2.71","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:71:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.71","text":"विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निःस्पृहः ।\nनिर्ममो निरहंकारः स शांतिमधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"vihāya kāmānyaḥ sarvānpumāṃścarati niḥspṛhaḥ |\nnirmamo nirahaṃkāraḥ sa śāṃtimadhigacchati ||","body":"Whoso forsaketh all desires and goeth onwards free from yearnings, selfless and without egoism—he goeth to Peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","71 of 72"]]},"g2-2-71":{"route":"#/gitav/2.71","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:71:en2","title":"Gita 2.71, in another translation","body":"That man who lives devoid of longing, abandoning all desires, without the sense of 'I' and 'mine,' he attains to peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","71 of 72"]]},"gv-2-72":{"route":"#/gitav/2.72","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:72:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 2.72","text":"एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति ।\nस्थित्वाऽस्यामन्तकालेऽपि ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"eṣā brāhmī sthitiḥ pārtha naināṃ prāpya vimuhyati |\nsthitvā’syāmantakāle’pi brahmanirvāṇamṛcchati ||","body":"This is the Eternal state, O son of Prithâ. Having attained thereto, none is bewildered. Who, even at the death-hour, is established therein, he goeth to the Nirvâna of the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","72 of 72"]]},"g2-2-72":{"route":"#/gitav/2.72","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 2 — The Way of Knowledge","src":"gita:2:72:en2","title":"Gita 2.72, in another translation","body":"This is to have one's being in Brahman, O son of Prithâ. None, attaining to this, becomes deluded. Being established therein, even at the end of life, a man attains to oneness with Brahman.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Knowledge"],["Verse","72 of 72"]]},"gv-3-1":{"route":"#/gitav/3.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:1:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.1","text":"ज्यायसी चेत्कर्मणस्ते मता बुद्धिर्जनार्दन ।\nतत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"jyāyasī cetkarmaṇaste matā buddhirjanārdana |\ntatkiṃ karmaṇi ghore māṃ niyojayasi keśava ||","body":"Arjuna said: If it be thought by Thee that knowledge is superior to action, O Janârdana, why dost Thou, O Keshava, enjoin on me this terrible action?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","1 of 43"]]},"g2-3-1":{"route":"#/gitav/3.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:1:en2","title":"Gita 3.1, in another translation","body":"If, O Janârdana, according to Thee, knowledge is superior to action, why then, O Keshava, dost Thou engage me in this terrible action?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","1 of 43"]]},"gv-3-2":{"route":"#/gitav/3.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:2:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.2","text":"व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव मे ।\nतदेकं वद निश्चित्य येन श्रेयोऽहमाप्नुयाम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"vyāmiśreṇeva vākyena buddhiṃ mohayasīva me |\ntadekaṃ vada niścitya yena śreyo’hamāpnuyām ||","body":"With these perplexing words Thou only confusest my understanding; therefore tell me with certainty the one way by which I may reach bliss.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","2 of 43"]]},"g2-3-2":{"route":"#/gitav/3.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:2:en2","title":"Gita 3.2, in another translation","body":"With these seemingly conflicting words, Thou art, as it were, bewildering my understanding;—tell me that one thing for certain, by which I can attain to the highest.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","2 of 43"]]},"gv-3-3":{"route":"#/gitav/3.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:3:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.3","text":"लोकेऽस्मिन्द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयानघ ।\nज्ञानयोगेन सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेन योगिनाम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"loke’smindvividhā niṣṭhā purā proktā mayānagha |\njñānayogena sāṃkhyānāṃ karmayogena yoginām ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: In this world there is a twofold path, as I before said, O sinless one: that of yoga by knowledge, of the Sâñkhyas; and that of yoga by action, of the Yogis.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","3 of 43"]]},"g2-3-3":{"route":"#/gitav/3.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:3:en2","title":"Gita 3.3, in another translation","body":"In the beginning (of creation), O sinless one, the twofold path of devotion was given by Me to this world;—the path of knowledge for the meditative, the path of work for the active.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","3 of 43"]]},"gv-3-4":{"route":"#/gitav/3.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:4:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.4","text":"न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्नुते ।\nन च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na karmaṇāmanārambhānnaiṣkarmyaṃ puruṣo’śnute |\nna ca saṃnyasanādeva siddhiṃ samadhigacchati ||","body":"Man winneth not freedom from action by abstaining from activity, nor by mere renunciation doth he rise to perfection.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","4 of 43"]]},"g2-3-4":{"route":"#/gitav/3.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:4:en2","title":"Gita 3.4, in another translation","body":"By non-performance of work none reaches worklessness; by merely giving up action no one attains to perfection.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","4 of 43"]]},"gv-3-5":{"route":"#/gitav/3.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:5:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.5","text":"न हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत् ।\nकार्यते ह्यवशः कर्म सर्वः प्रकृतिजैर्गुणैः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na hi kaścitkṣaṇamapi jātu tiṣṭhatyakarmakṛt |\nkāryate hyavaśaḥ karma sarvaḥ prakṛtijairguṇaiḥ ||","body":"Nor can anyone, even for an instant, remain really actionless; for helplessly is everyone driven to action by the qualities born of nature.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","5 of 43"]]},"g2-3-5":{"route":"#/gitav/3.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:5:en2","title":"Gita 3.5, in another translation","body":"Verily none can ever rest for even an instant, without performing action; for all are made to act, helplessly indeed, by the Gunas, born of Prakriti.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","5 of 43"]]},"gv-3-6":{"route":"#/gitav/3.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:6:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.6","text":"कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य य आस्ते मनसा स्मरन् ।\nइन्द्रियार्थान्विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmendriyāṇi saṃyamya ya āste manasā smaran |\nindriyārthānvimūḍhātmā mithyācāraḥ sa ucyate ||","body":"Who sitteth, controlling the organs of action, but dwelling in his mind on the objects of the senses, that bewildered man is called a hypocrite.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","6 of 43"]]},"g2-3-6":{"route":"#/gitav/3.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:6:en2","title":"Gita 3.6, in another translation","body":"He, who restraining the organs of action, sits revolving in the mind, thoughts regarding objects of senses, he, of deluded understanding, is called a hypocrite.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","6 of 43"]]},"gv-3-7":{"route":"#/gitav/3.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:7:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.7","text":"यस्त्विन्द्रियाणि मनसा नियम्यारभतेऽर्जुन ।\nकर्मेन्द्रियैः कर्मयोगमसक्तः स विशिष्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yastvindriyāṇi manasā niyamyārabhate’rjuna |\nkarmendriyaiḥ karmayogamasaktaḥ sa viśiṣyate ||","body":"But who, controlling the senses by the mind, O Arjuna, with the organs of action without attachment, performeth yoga by action, he is worthy.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","7 of 43"]]},"g2-3-7":{"route":"#/gitav/3.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:7:en2","title":"Gita 3.7, in another translation","body":"But, who, controlling the senses by the mind, unattached, directs his organs of action to the path of work, he, O Arjuna, excels.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","7 of 43"]]},"gv-3-8":{"route":"#/gitav/3.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:8:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.8","text":"नियतं कुरु कर्म त्वं कर्म ज्यायो ह्यकर्मणः ।\nशरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिद्ध्येदकर्मणः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"niyataṃ kuru karma tvaṃ karma jyāyo hyakarmaṇaḥ |\nśarīrayātrāpi ca te na prasiddhyedakarmaṇaḥ ||","body":"Perform thou right action, for, action is superior to inaction, and, inactive, even the maintenance of thy body would not be possible.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","8 of 43"]]},"g2-3-8":{"route":"#/gitav/3.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:8:en2","title":"Gita 3.8, in another translation","body":"Do thou perform obligatory action; for action is superior to inaction, and even the bare maintenance of thy body would not be possible if thou art inactive.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","8 of 43"]]},"gv-3-9":{"route":"#/gitav/3.9","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:9:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.9","text":"यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः ।\nतदर्थं कर्म कौन्तेय मुक्तसंगः समाचर ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yajñārthātkarmaṇo’nyatra loko’yaṃ karmabandhanaḥ |\ntadarthaṃ karma kaunteya muktasaṃgaḥ samācara ||","body":"The world is bound by action, unless performed for the sake of sacrifice; for that sake, free from attachment, O son of Kuntî, perform thou action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","9 of 43"]]},"g2-3-9":{"route":"#/gitav/3.9","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:9:en2","title":"Gita 3.9, in another translation","body":"The world is bound by actions other than those performed for the sake of Yajna; do thou therefore, O son of Kunti, perform action for Yajna alone, devoid of attachment.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","9 of 43"]]},"gv-3-10":{"route":"#/gitav/3.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:10:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.10","text":"सहयज्ञाः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा पुरोवाच प्रजापतिः ।\nअनेन प्रसविष्यध्वमेष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sahayajñāḥ prajāḥ sṛṣṭvā purovāca prajāpatiḥ |\nanena prasaviṣyadhvameṣa vo’stviṣṭakāmadhuk ||","body":"Having in ancient times emanated mankind together with sacrifice, the Lord of emanation said: \"By this shall ye propagate; be this to you the giver of desire;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","10 of 43"]]},"g2-3-10":{"route":"#/gitav/3.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:10:en2","title":"Gita 3.10, in another translation","body":"The Prajâpati, having in the beginning created mankind together with Yajna, said,—\"By this shall ye multiply: this shall be the milch cow of your desires.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","10 of 43"]]},"gv-3-11":{"route":"#/gitav/3.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:11:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.11","text":"देवान्भावयतानेन ते देवा भावयन्तु वः ।\nपरस्परं भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"devānbhāvayatānena te devā bhāvayantu vaḥ |\nparasparaṃ bhāvayantaḥ śreyaḥ paramavāpsyatha ||","body":"\"With this nourish ye the Shining Ones, and may the Shining Ones nourish you; thus nourishing one another ye shall reap the supremest good.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","11 of 43"]]},"g2-3-11":{"route":"#/gitav/3.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:11:en2","title":"Gita 3.11, in another translation","body":"\"Cherish the Devas with this, and may those Devas cherish you: thus cherishing one another, ye shall gain the highest good.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","11 of 43"]]},"gv-3-12":{"route":"#/gitav/3.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:12:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.12","text":"इष्टान्भोगान्हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः ।\nतैर्दत्तानप्रदायैभ्यो यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"iṣṭānbhogānhi vo devā dāsyante yajñabhāvitāḥ |\ntairdattānapradāyaibhyo yo bhuṅkte stena eva saḥ ||","body":"\"For, nourished by sacrifice, the Shining Ones shall bestow on you the enjoyments you desire.\" A thief verily is he who enjoyeth what is given by Them without returning Them aught.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","12 of 43"]]},"g2-3-12":{"route":"#/gitav/3.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:12:en2","title":"Gita 3.12, in another translation","body":"\"The Devas, cherished by Yajna, will give you desired-for objects.\" So, he who enjoys objects given by the Devas without offering (in return) to them, is verily a thief.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","12 of 43"]]},"gv-3-13":{"route":"#/gitav/3.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:13:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.13","text":"यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः ।\nभुञ्जते ते त्वघं पापा ये पचन्त्यात्मकारणात् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yajñaśiṣṭāśinaḥ santo mucyante sarvakilbiṣaiḥ |\nbhuñjate te tvaghaṃ pāpā ye pacantyātmakāraṇāt ||","body":"The righteous, who eat the remains of the sacrifice, are freed from all sins; but the impious, who dress food for their own sakes, they verily eat sin.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","13 of 43"]]},"g2-3-13":{"route":"#/gitav/3.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:13:en2","title":"Gita 3.13, in another translation","body":"The good, eating the remnants of Yajna, are freed from all sins: but who cook food (only) for themselves, those sinful ones eat sin.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","13 of 43"]]},"gv-3-14":{"route":"#/gitav/3.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:14:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.14","text":"अन्नाद्भवन्ति भूतानि पर्जन्यादन्नसम्भवः ।\nयज्ञाद्भवति पर्जन्यो यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"annādbhavanti bhūtāni parjanyādannasambhavaḥ |\nyajñādbhavati parjanyo yajñaḥ karmasamudbhavaḥ ||","body":"From food creatures become; from rain is the production of food; rain proceedeth from sacrifice; sacrifice ariseth out of action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","14 of 43"]]},"g2-3-14":{"route":"#/gitav/3.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:14:en2","title":"Gita 3.14, in another translation","body":"From food come forth beings: from rain food is produced: from Yajna arises rain and Yajna is born of Karma.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","14 of 43"]]},"gv-3-15":{"route":"#/gitav/3.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:15:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.15","text":"कर्म ब्रह्मोद्भवं विद्धि ब्रह्माक्षरसमुद्भवम् ।\nतस्मात्सर्वगतं ब्रह्म नित्यं यज्ञे प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karma brahmodbhavaṃ viddhi brahmākṣarasamudbhavam |\ntasmātsarvagataṃ brahma nityaṃ yajñe pratiṣṭhitam ||","body":"Know thou that from Brahma action groweth, and Brahma from the Imperishable cometh. Therefore the Eternal, the all-permeating, is ever present in sacrifice.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","15 of 43"]]},"g2-3-15":{"route":"#/gitav/3.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:15:en2","title":"Gita 3.15, in another translation","body":"Know Karma to have risen from the Veda, and the Veda from the Imperishable. Therefore the all-pervading Veda is ever centred in Yajna.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","15 of 43"]]},"gv-3-16":{"route":"#/gitav/3.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:16:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.16","text":"एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं नानुवर्तयतीह यः ।\nअघायुरिन्द्रियारामो मोघं पार्थ स जीवति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"evaṃ pravartitaṃ cakraṃ nānuvartayatīha yaḥ |\naghāyurindriyārāmo moghaṃ pārtha sa jīvati ||","body":"He who on earth doth not follow the wheel thus revolving, sinful of life and rejoicing in the senses, he, O son of Pritha, liveth in vain.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","16 of 43"]]},"g2-3-16":{"route":"#/gitav/3.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:16:en2","title":"Gita 3.16, in another translation","body":"He, who here follows not the wheel thus set revolving, living in sin, and satisfied in the senses, O son of Prithâ,—he lives in vain.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","16 of 43"]]},"gv-3-17":{"route":"#/gitav/3.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:17:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.17","text":"यस्त्वात्मरतिरेव स्यादात्मतृप्तश्च मानवः ।\nआत्मन्येव च सन्तुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yastvātmaratireva syādātmatṛptaśca mānavaḥ |\nātmanyeva ca santuṣṭastasya kāryaṃ na vidyate ||","body":"But the man who rejoiceth in the Self, with the Self is satisfied, and is content in the Self, for him verily there is nothing to do;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","17 of 43"]]},"g2-3-17":{"route":"#/gitav/3.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:17:en2","title":"Gita 3.17, in another translation","body":"But the man who is devoted to the Self, and is satisfied with the Self, and content in the Self alone, he has no obligatory duty.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","17 of 43"]]},"gv-3-18":{"route":"#/gitav/3.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:18:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.18","text":"नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन ।\nन चास्य सर्वभूतेषु कश्चिदर्थव्यपाश्रयः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"naiva tasya kṛtenārtho nākṛteneha kaścana |\nna cāsya sarvabhūteṣu kaścidarthavyapāśrayaḥ ||","body":"For him there is no interest in things done, in this world, nor any in things not done, nor doth any object of his depend on any being.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","18 of 43"]]},"g2-3-18":{"route":"#/gitav/3.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:18:en2","title":"Gita 3.18, in another translation","body":"He has no object in this world (to gain) by doing (an action), nor (does he incur any loss) by non-performance of action,—nor has he (need of) depending on any being for any object.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","18 of 43"]]},"gv-3-19":{"route":"#/gitav/3.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:19:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.19","text":"तस्मादसक्तः सततं कार्यं कर्म समाचर ।\nअसक्तो ह्याचरन्कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tasmādasaktaḥ satataṃ kāryaṃ karma samācara |\nasakto hyācarankarma paramāpnoti pūruṣaḥ ||","body":"Therefore, without attachment, constantly perform action which is duty, for, by performing action without attachment, man verily reacheth the Supreme.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","19 of 43"]]},"g2-3-19":{"route":"#/gitav/3.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:19:en2","title":"Gita 3.19, in another translation","body":"Therefore, do thou always perform actions which are obligatory, without attachment;—by performing action without attachment, one attains to the highest.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","19 of 43"]]},"gv-3-20":{"route":"#/gitav/3.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:20:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.20","text":"कर्मणैव हि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः ।\nलोकसंग्रहमेवापि संपश्यन्कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmaṇaiva hi saṃsiddhimāsthitā janakādayaḥ |\nlokasaṃgrahamevāpi saṃpaśyankartumarhasi ||","body":"Janaka and others indeed attained to perfection by action: then having an eye to the welfare of he world also, thou shouldst perform action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","20 of 43"]]},"g2-3-20":{"route":"#/gitav/3.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:20:en2","title":"Gita 3.20, in another translation","body":"Verily by action alone, Janaka and others attained perfection;—also, simply with the view for the guidance of men, thou shouldst perform action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","20 of 43"]]},"gv-3-21":{"route":"#/gitav/3.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:21:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.21","text":"यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः ।\nस यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadyadācarati śreṣṭhastattadevetaro janaḥ |\nsa yatpramāṇaṃ kurute lokastadanuvartate ||","body":"Whatsoever a great man doeth, that other men also do; the standard he setteth up, by that the people go.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","21 of 43"]]},"g2-3-21":{"route":"#/gitav/3.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:21:en2","title":"Gita 3.21, in another translation","body":"Whatsoever the superior person does, that is followed by others. What he demonstrates by action, that, people follow.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","21 of 43"]]},"gv-3-22":{"route":"#/gitav/3.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:22:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.22","text":"न मे पार्थास्ति कर्तव्यं त्रिषु लोकेषु किञ्चन ।\nनानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यं वर्त एव च कर्मणि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na me pārthāsti kartavyaṃ triṣu lokeṣu kiñcana |\nnānavāptamavāptavyaṃ varta eva ca karmaṇi ||","body":"There is nothing in the three worlds, O Pârtha, that should be done by Me, nor anything unattained that might be attained; yet I mingle in action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","22 of 43"]]},"g2-3-22":{"route":"#/gitav/3.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:22:en2","title":"Gita 3.22, in another translation","body":"I have, O son of Prithâ, no duty, nothing that I have not gained, and nothing that I have to gain, in the three worlds; yet, I continue in action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","22 of 43"]]},"gv-3-23":{"route":"#/gitav/3.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:23:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.23","text":"यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadi hyahaṃ na varteyaṃ jātu karmaṇyatandritaḥ |\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ ||","body":"For if I mingled not ever in action unwearied, men all around would follow My path, O son of Prithâ.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","23 of 43"]]},"g2-3-23":{"route":"#/gitav/3.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:23:en2","title":"Gita 3.23, in another translation","body":"If ever I did not continue in work, without relaxation, men, O son of Prithâ, would in every way, follow in My wake.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","23 of 43"]]},"gv-3-24":{"route":"#/gitav/3.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:24:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.24","text":"उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम् ।\nसङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"utsīdeyurime lokā na kuryāṃ karma cedaham |\nsaṅkarasya ca kartā syāmupahanyāmimāḥ prajāḥ ||","body":"These worlds would fall into ruin, if I did not perform action; I should be the author of confusion of castes, and should destroy these creatures.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","24 of 43"]]},"g2-3-24":{"route":"#/gitav/3.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:24:en2","title":"Gita 3.24, in another translation","body":"If I did not do work, these worlds would perish. I should be the cause of the admixture of races, and I should ruin these beings.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","24 of 43"]]},"gv-3-25":{"route":"#/gitav/3.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:25:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.25","text":"सक्ताः कर्मण्यविद्वांसो यथा कुर्वन्ति भारत ।\nकुर्याद्विद्वांस्तथासक्तश्चिकीर्षुर्लोकसंग्रहम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"saktāḥ karmaṇyavidvāṃso yathā kurvanti bhārata |\nkuryādvidvāṃstathāsaktaścikīrṣurlokasaṃgraham ||","body":"As the ignorant act from attachment to action, O Bhârata, so should the wise act without attachment, desiring the welfare of the world.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","25 of 43"]]},"g2-3-25":{"route":"#/gitav/3.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:25:en2","title":"Gita 3.25, in another translation","body":"As do the unwise, attached to work, act, so should the wise act, O descendant of Bharata, (but) without attachment, desirous of the guidance of the world.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","25 of 43"]]},"gv-3-26":{"route":"#/gitav/3.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:26:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.26","text":"न बुद्धिभेदं जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् ।\nजोषयेत्सर्वकर्माणि विद्वान् युक्तः समाचरन् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na buddhibhedaṃ janayedajñānāṃ karmasaṅginām |\njoṣayetsarvakarmāṇi vidvān yuktaḥ samācaran ||","body":"Let no wise man unsettle the mind of ignorant people attached to action; but acting in harmony with Me let him render all action attractive.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","26 of 43"]]},"g2-3-26":{"route":"#/gitav/3.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:26:en2","title":"Gita 3.26, in another translation","body":"One should not unsettle the understanding of the ignorant, attached to action; the wise, (himself) steadily acting, should engage (the ignorant) in all work.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","26 of 43"]]},"gv-3-27":{"route":"#/gitav/3.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:27:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.27","text":"प्रकृतेः क्रियमाणानि गुणैः कर्माणि सर्वशः ।\nअहङ्कारविमूढात्मा कर्ताऽहमिति मन्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"prakṛteḥ kriyamāṇāni guṇaiḥ karmāṇi sarvaśaḥ |\nahaṅkāravimūḍhātmā kartā’hamiti manyate ||","body":"All actions are wrought by the quali ties of nature only. The self, deluded by egoism, thinketh: \"I am the doer.\"","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","27 of 43"]]},"g2-3-27":{"route":"#/gitav/3.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:27:en2","title":"Gita 3.27, in another translation","body":"The Gunas of Prakriti perform all action. With the understanding deluded by egoism, man thinks, \"I am the doer.\"","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","27 of 43"]]},"gv-3-28":{"route":"#/gitav/3.28","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:28:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.28","text":"तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः ।\nगुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्त इति मत्वा न सज्जते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tattvavittu mahābāho guṇakarmavibhāgayoḥ |\nguṇā guṇeṣu vartanta iti matvā na sajjate ||","body":"But he, O mighty-armed, who knoweth the essence of the divisions of the qualities and functions, holding that \"the qualities move amid the qualities,\" is not attached.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","28 of 43"]]},"g2-3-28":{"route":"#/gitav/3.28","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:28:en2","title":"Gita 3.28, in another translation","body":"But, one, with true insight into the domains of Guna and Karma, knowing that Gunas as senses merely rest on Gunas as objects, does not become attached.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","28 of 43"]]},"gv-3-29":{"route":"#/gitav/3.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:29:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.29","text":"प्रकृतेर्गुणसम्मूढाः सज्जन्ते गुणकर्मसु ।\nतानकृत्स्नविदो मन्दान्कृत्स्नविन्न विचालयेत् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"prakṛterguṇasammūḍhāḥ sajjante guṇakarmasu |\ntānakṛtsnavido mandānkṛtsnavinna vicālayet ||","body":"Those deluded by the qualities of nature are attached to the functions of the qualities. The man of perfect knowledge should not unsettle the foolish whose knowledge is imperfect.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","29 of 43"]]},"g2-3-29":{"route":"#/gitav/3.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:29:en2","title":"Gita 3.29, in another translation","body":"Men of perfect knowledge should not unsettle (the understanding of) people of dull wit and imperfect knowledge, who deluded by the Gunas of Prakriti attach (themselves) to the functions of the Gunas.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","29 of 43"]]},"gv-3-30":{"route":"#/gitav/3.30","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:30:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.30","text":"मयि सर्वाणि कर्माणि संन्यस्याध्यात्मचेतसा ।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा युध्यस्व विगतज्वरः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"mayi sarvāṇi karmāṇi saṃnyasyādhyātmacetasā |\nnirāśīrnirmamo bhūtvā yudhyasva vigatajvaraḥ ||","body":"Surrendering all actions to Me, with thy thoughts resting on the supreme Self, from hope and egoism freed, and of mental fever cured, engage in battle.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","30 of 43"]]},"g2-3-30":{"route":"#/gitav/3.30","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:30:en2","title":"Gita 3.30, in another translation","body":"Renouncing all actions to Me, with mind centred on the Self, getting rid of hope and selfishness, fight,—free from (mental) fever.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","30 of 43"]]},"gv-3-31":{"route":"#/gitav/3.31","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:31:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.31","text":"ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ।\nश्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ye me matamidaṃ nityamanutiṣṭhanti mānavāḥ |\nśraddhāvanto’nasūyanto mucyante te’pi karmabhiḥ ||","body":"Who abide ever in this teaching of Mine full of faith and free from caviling, they too are released from actions.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","31 of 43"]]},"g2-3-31":{"route":"#/gitav/3.31","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:31:en2","title":"Gita 3.31, in another translation","body":"Those men who constantly practise this teaching of Mine, full of Shraddhâ and without cavilling, they too, are freed from work.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","31 of 43"]]},"gv-3-32":{"route":"#/gitav/3.32","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:32:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.32","text":"ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम् ।\nसर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ye tvetadabhyasūyanto nānutiṣṭhanti me matam |\nsarvajñānavimūḍhāṃstānviddhi naṣṭānacetasaḥ ||","body":"Who carp at My teaching and act not thereon, senseless, deluded in all knowledge, know thou these mindless ones as fated to be destroyed.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","32 of 43"]]},"g2-3-32":{"route":"#/gitav/3.32","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:32:en2","title":"Gita 3.32, in another translation","body":"But those who decrying this teaching of Mine do not practise (it), deluded in all knowledge, and devoid of discrimination, know them to be ruined.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","32 of 43"]]},"gv-3-33":{"route":"#/gitav/3.33","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:33:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.33","text":"सदृशं चेष्टते स्वस्याः प्रकृतेर्ज्ञानवानपि ।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि निग्रहः किं करिष्यति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sadṛśaṃ ceṣṭate svasyāḥ prakṛterjñānavānapi |\nprakṛtiṃ yānti bhūtāni nigrahaḥ kiṃ kariṣyati ||","body":"Even the man of knowledge behaves in conformity with his own nature; beings follow nature; what shall restraint avail?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","33 of 43"]]},"g2-3-33":{"route":"#/gitav/3.33","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:33:en2","title":"Gita 3.33, in another translation","body":"Even a wise man acts in accordance with his own nature: beings follow nature: what can restraint do?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","33 of 43"]]},"gv-3-34":{"route":"#/gitav/3.34","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:34:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.34","text":"इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ ।\nतयोर्न वशमागच्छेत्तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"indriyasyendriyasyārthe rāgadveṣau vyavasthitau |\ntayorna vaśamāgacchettau hyasya paripanthinau ||","body":"Affection and aversion for the objects of sense abide in the senses; let none come under the dominion of these two; they are obstructors of the path.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","34 of 43"]]},"g2-3-34":{"route":"#/gitav/3.34","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:34:en2","title":"Gita 3.34, in another translation","body":"Attachment and aversion of the senses for their respective objects are natural: let none come under their sway: they are his foes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","34 of 43"]]},"gv-3-35":{"route":"#/gitav/3.35","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:35:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.35","text":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śreyānsvadharmo viguṇaḥ paradharmātsvanuṣṭhitāt |\nsvadharme nidhanaṃ śreyaḥ paradharmo bhayāvahaḥ ||","body":"Better one's own duty, though destitute of merit, than the duty of another, well discharged. Better death in the discharge of one's own duty; the duty of another is full of danger.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","35 of 43"]]},"g2-3-35":{"route":"#/gitav/3.35","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:35:en2","title":"Gita 3.35, in another translation","body":"Better is one's own Dharma, (though) imperfect, than the Dharma of another well-performed. Better is death in one's own Dharma: the Dharma of another is fraught with fear.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","35 of 43"]]},"gv-3-36":{"route":"#/gitav/3.36","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:36:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.36","text":"अथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः ।\nअनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय बलादिव नियोजितः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"atha kena prayukto’yaṃ pāpaṃ carati pūruṣaḥ |\nanicchannapi vārṣṇeya balādiva niyojitaḥ ||","body":"Arjuna said: But dragged on by what does a man commit sin, reluctantly indeed, O Varshneya, as it were by force constrained?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","36 of 43"]]},"g2-3-36":{"route":"#/gitav/3.36","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:36:en2","title":"Gita 3.36, in another translation","body":"But by what impelled does man commit sin, though against his wishes, O Vârshneya, constrained as it were, by force?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","36 of 43"]]},"gv-3-37":{"route":"#/gitav/3.37","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:37:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.37","text":"काम एष क्रोध एष रजोगुणसमुद्भवः ।\nमहाशनो महापाप्मा विद्ध्येनमिह वैरिणम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kāma eṣa krodha eṣa rajoguṇasamudbhavaḥ |\nmahāśano mahāpāpmā viddhyenamiha vairiṇam ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: It is desire, it is wrath, begotten by the quality of motion; all-consuming, all-polluting, know thou this as our foe here on earth.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","37 of 43"]]},"g2-3-37":{"route":"#/gitav/3.37","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:37:en2","title":"Gita 3.37, in another translation","body":"It is desire—it is anger, born of the Rajo-guna: of great craving, and of great sin; know this as the foe here (in this world).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","37 of 43"]]},"gv-3-38":{"route":"#/gitav/3.38","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:38:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.38","text":"धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निर्यथाऽऽदर्शो मलेन च ।\nयथोल्बेनावृतो गर्भस्तथा तेनेदमावृतम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"dhūmenāvriyate vahniryathā’’darśo malena ca |\nyatholbenāvṛto garbhastathā tenedamāvṛtam ||","body":"As a flame is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror by dust, as an embryo is wrapped by the amnion, so This is enveloped by it.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","38 of 43"]]},"g2-3-38":{"route":"#/gitav/3.38","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:38:en2","title":"Gita 3.38, in another translation","body":"As fire is enveloped by smoke, as a mirror by dust, as an embryo by the secundine, so is it covered by that.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","38 of 43"]]},"gv-3-39":{"route":"#/gitav/3.39","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:39:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.39","text":"आवृतं ज्ञानमेतेन ज्ञानिनो नित्यवैरिणा ।\nकामरूपेण कौन्तेय दुष्पूरेणानलेन च ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"āvṛtaṃ jñānametena jñānino nityavairiṇā |\nkāmarūpeṇa kaunteya duṣpūreṇānalena ca ||","body":"Enveloped is wisdom by this constant enemy of the wise in the form of desire, which is insatiable as a flame.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","39 of 43"]]},"g2-3-39":{"route":"#/gitav/3.39","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:39:en2","title":"Gita 3.39, in another translation","body":"Knowledge is covered by this, the constant foe of the wise, O son of Kunti, the unappeasable fire of desire.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","39 of 43"]]},"gv-3-40":{"route":"#/gitav/3.40","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:40:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.40","text":"इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते ।\nएतैर्विमोहयत्येष ज्ञानमावृत्य देहिनम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"indriyāṇi mano buddhirasyādhiṣṭhānamucyate |\netairvimohayatyeṣa jñānamāvṛtya dehinam ||","body":"The senses, the mind and the Reason are said to be its seat; by these enveloping wisdom, it bewilders the dweller in the body.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","40 of 43"]]},"g2-3-40":{"route":"#/gitav/3.40","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:40:en2","title":"Gita 3.40, in another translation","body":"The senses, the mind and the intellect are said to be its abode: through these, it deludes the embodied by veiling his wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","40 of 43"]]},"gv-3-41":{"route":"#/gitav/3.41","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:41:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.41","text":"तस्मात्त्वमिन्द्रियाण्यादौ नियम्य भरतर्षभ ।\nपाप्मानं प्रजहि ह्येनं ज्ञानविज्ञाननाशनम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tasmāttvamindriyāṇyādau niyamya bharatarṣabha |\npāpmānaṃ prajahi hyenaṃ jñānavijñānanāśanam ||","body":"Therefore, O best of the Bhâratas, mastering first the senses, do thou slay this thing of sin, destructive of wisdom and knowledge.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","41 of 43"]]},"g2-3-41":{"route":"#/gitav/3.41","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:41:en2","title":"Gita 3.41, in another translation","body":"Therefore, O Bull of the Bharata race, controlling the senses at the outset, kill it,—the sinful, the destroyer of knowledge and realisation.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","41 of 43"]]},"gv-3-42":{"route":"#/gitav/3.42","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:42:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.42","text":"इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः ।\nमनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"indriyāṇi parāṇyāhurindriyebhyaḥ paraṃ manaḥ |\nmanasastu parā buddhiryo buddheḥ paratastu saḥ ||","body":"It is said that the senses are great; greater than the senses is the mind: greater than the mind is the Reason; but what is greater than the Reason, is He.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","42 of 43"]]},"g2-3-42":{"route":"#/gitav/3.42","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:42:en2","title":"Gita 3.42, in another translation","body":"The senses are said to be superior (to the body); the mind is superior to the senses; the intellect is superior to the mind; and that which is superior to the intellect is He (the Atman).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","42 of 43"]]},"gv-3-43":{"route":"#/gitav/3.43","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:43:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 3.43","text":"एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nजहि शत्रुं महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"evaṃ buddheḥ paraṃ buddhvā saṃstabhyātmānamātmanā |\njahi śatruṃ mahābāho kāmarūpaṃ durāsadam ||","body":"Thus understanding Him as greater than the Reason, restraining the self by the Self, slay thou, O mighty-armed, the enemy in the form of desire, difficult to overcome.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","43 of 43"]]},"g2-3-43":{"route":"#/gitav/3.43","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 3 — The Way of Action","src":"gita:3:43:en2","title":"Gita 3.43, in another translation","body":"Thus, knowing Him who is superior to the intellect, and restraining the self by the Self, destroy, O mighty-armed, that enemy, the unseizable foe, desire.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Action"],["Verse","43 of 43"]]},"gv-4-1":{"route":"#/gitav/4.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:1:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.1","text":"इमं विवस्वते योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम् ।\nविवस्वान् मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"imaṃ vivasvate yogaṃ proktavānahamavyayam |\nvivasvān manave prāha manurikṣvākave’bravīt ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: This imperishable yoga I declared to Vivasvân; Vivasvân taught it to Manu; Manu to Ikshvâku told it.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","1 of 42"]]},"g2-4-1":{"route":"#/gitav/4.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:1:en2","title":"Gita 4.1, in another translation","body":"I told this imperishable Yoga to Vivasvat; Vivasvat told it to Manu; (and) Manu told it to Ikshvâku:","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","1 of 42"]]},"gv-4-2":{"route":"#/gitav/4.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:2:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.2","text":"एवं परम्पराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो विदुः ।\nस कालेनेह महता योगो नष्टः परन्तप ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"evaṃ paramparāprāptamimaṃ rājarṣayo viduḥ |\nsa kāleneha mahatā yogo naṣṭaḥ parantapa ||","body":"This, handed on down the line, the King-Sages knew. This yoga by great efflux of time decayed in the world, O Parantapa.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","2 of 42"]]},"g2-4-2":{"route":"#/gitav/4.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:2:en2","title":"Gita 4.2, in another translation","body":"Thus handed down in regular succession, the royal sages knew it. This Yoga, by long lapse of time, declined in this world, O burner of foes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","2 of 42"]]},"gv-4-3":{"route":"#/gitav/4.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:3:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.3","text":"स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः ।\nभक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sa evāyaṃ mayā te’dya yogaḥ proktaḥ purātanaḥ |\nbhakto’si me sakhā ceti rahasyaṃ hyetaduttamam ||","body":"This same ancient yoga hath been to-day declared to thee by Me, for thou art My devotee and My friend; it is the supreme Secret.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","3 of 42"]]},"g2-4-3":{"route":"#/gitav/4.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:3:en2","title":"Gita 4.3, in another translation","body":"I have this day told thee that same ancient Yoga, (for) thou art My devotee, and My friend, and this secret is profound indeed.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","3 of 42"]]},"gv-4-4":{"route":"#/gitav/4.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:4:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.4","text":"अपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः ।\nकथमेतद्विजानीयां त्वमादौ प्रोक्तवानिति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"aparaṃ bhavato janma paraṃ janma vivasvataḥ |\nkathametadvijānīyāṃ tvamādau proktavāniti ||","body":"Arjuna said: Later was Thy birth, earlier the birth of Vivasvân; how then am I to understand that Thou declaredst it in the beginning?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","4 of 42"]]},"g2-4-4":{"route":"#/gitav/4.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:4:en2","title":"Gita 4.4, in another translation","body":"Later was Thy birth, and that of Vivasvat prior; how then should I understand that Thou toldest this in the beginning?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","4 of 42"]]},"gv-4-5":{"route":"#/gitav/4.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:5:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.5","text":"बहूनि मे व्यतीतानि जन्मानि तव चार्जुन ।\nतान्यहं वेद सर्वाणि न त्वं वेत्थ परन्तप ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"bahūni me vyatītāni janmāni tava cārjuna |\ntānyahaṃ veda sarvāṇi na tvaṃ vettha parantapa ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: Many births have been left behind by Me and by thee, O Arjuna. I know them all, but thou knowest not thine, O Parantapa.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","5 of 42"]]},"g2-4-5":{"route":"#/gitav/4.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:5:en2","title":"Gita 4.5, in another translation","body":"Many are the births that have been passed by Me and thee, O Arjuna. I know them all, whilst thou knowest not, O scorcher of foes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","5 of 42"]]},"gv-4-6":{"route":"#/gitav/4.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:6:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.6","text":"अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा भूतानामीश्वरोऽपि सन् ।\nप्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय संभवाम्यात्ममायया ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ajo’pi sannavyayātmā bhūtānāmīśvaro’pi san |\nprakṛtiṃ svāmadhiṣṭhāya saṃbhavāmyātmamāyayā ||","body":"Though unborn, the imperishable Self, and also the Lord of all beings, brooding over nature which is Mine own, yet I am born through My own Power.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","6 of 42"]]},"g2-4-6":{"route":"#/gitav/4.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:6:en2","title":"Gita 4.6, in another translation","body":"Though I am unborn, of changeless nature and Lord of beings, yet subjugating My Prakriti, I come into being by My own Mâyâ.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","6 of 42"]]},"gv-4-7":{"route":"#/gitav/4.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:7:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.7","text":"यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदाऽऽत्मानं सृजाम्यहम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadā yadā hi dharmasya glānirbhavati bhārata |\nabhyutthānamadharmasya tadā’’tmānaṃ sṛjāmyaham ||","body":"Whenever there is decay of righteousness, O Bhârata, and there is exaltation of unrighteousness, then I Myself come forth;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","7 of 42"]]},"g2-4-7":{"route":"#/gitav/4.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:7:en2","title":"Gita 4.7, in another translation","body":"Whenever, O descendant of Bharata, there is decline of Dharma, and rise of Adharma, then I body Myself forth.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","7 of 42"]]},"gv-4-8":{"route":"#/gitav/4.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:8:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.8","text":"परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम् ।\nधर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"paritrāṇāya sādhūnāṃ vināśāya ca duṣkṛtām |\ndharmasaṃsthāpanārthāya saṃbhavāmi yuge yuge ||","body":"For the protection of the good, for the destruction of evil-doers, for the sake of firmly establishing righteousness, I am born from age to age.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","8 of 42"]]},"g2-4-8":{"route":"#/gitav/4.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:8:en2","title":"Gita 4.8, in another translation","body":"For the protection of the good, for the destruction of the wicked, and for the establishment of Dharma, I come into being in every age.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","8 of 42"]]},"gv-4-9":{"route":"#/gitav/4.9","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:9:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.9","text":"जन्म कर्म च मे दिव्यमेवं यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nत्यक्त्वा देहं पुनर्जन्म नैति मामेति सोऽर्जुन ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"janma karma ca me divyamevaṃ yo vetti tattvataḥ |\ntyaktvā dehaṃ punarjanma naiti māmeti so’rjuna ||","body":"He who thus knoweth My divine birth and action, in its essence, having abandoned the body, cometh not to birth again, but cometh unto Me, O Arjuna.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","9 of 42"]]},"g2-4-9":{"route":"#/gitav/4.9","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:9:en2","title":"Gita 4.9, in another translation","body":"He who thus knows, in true light, My divine birth and action, leaving the body, is not born again: he attains to Me, O Arjuna.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","9 of 42"]]},"gv-4-10":{"route":"#/gitav/4.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:10:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.10","text":"वीतरागभयक्रोधा मन्मया मामुपाश्रिताः ।\nबहवो ज्ञानतपसा पूता मद्भावमागताः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"vītarāgabhayakrodhā manmayā māmupāśritāḥ |\nbahavo jñānatapasā pūtā madbhāvamāgatāḥ ||","body":"Freed from passion, fear and anger, filled with Me, taking refuge in Me, purified in the fire of wisdom, many have entered into My Being.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","10 of 42"]]},"g2-4-10":{"route":"#/gitav/4.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:10:en2","title":"Gita 4.10, in another translation","body":"Freed from attachment, fear and anger, absorbed in Me, taking refuge in Me, purified by the fire of Knowledge, many have attained My Being.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","10 of 42"]]},"gv-4-11":{"route":"#/gitav/4.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:11:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.11","text":"ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम् ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ye yathā māṃ prapadyante tāṃstathaiva bhajāmyaham |\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ ||","body":"However men approach Me, even so do I welcome them, for the path men take from every side is Mine, O Pârtha.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","11 of 42"]]},"g2-4-11":{"route":"#/gitav/4.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:11:en2","title":"Gita 4.11, in another translation","body":"In whatever way men worship Me, in the same way do I fulfil their desires: (it is) My path, O son of Prithâ, (that) men tread, in all ways.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","11 of 42"]]},"gv-4-12":{"route":"#/gitav/4.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:12:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.12","text":"काङ्क्षन्तः कर्मणां सिद्धिं यजन्त इह देवताः ।\nक्षिप्रं हि मानुषे लोके सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kāṅkṣantaḥ karmaṇāṃ siddhiṃ yajanta iha devatāḥ |\nkṣipraṃ hi mānuṣe loke siddhirbhavati karmajā ||","body":"They who long after success in action on earth worship the Shining Ones; for in brief space verily, in this world of men, success is born of action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","12 of 42"]]},"g2-4-12":{"route":"#/gitav/4.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:12:en2","title":"Gita 4.12, in another translation","body":"Longing for success in action, in this world, (men) worship the gods. Because success, resulting from action, is, quickly attained in the human world.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","12 of 42"]]},"gv-4-13":{"route":"#/gitav/4.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:13:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.13","text":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः ।\nतस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्ध्यकर्तारमव्ययम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"cāturvarṇyaṃ mayā sṛṣṭaṃ guṇakarmavibhāgaśaḥ |\ntasya kartāramapi māṃ viddhyakartāramavyayam ||","body":"The four castes were emanated by Me, by the different distribution of qualities and actions; know Me to be the author of them, though the actionless and inexhaustible.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","13 of 42"]]},"g2-4-13":{"route":"#/gitav/4.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:13:en2","title":"Gita 4.13, in another translation","body":"The fourfold caste was created by Me, by the differentiation of Guna and Karma. Though I am the author thereof, know Me to be the non-doer, and changeless.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","13 of 42"]]},"gv-4-14":{"route":"#/gitav/4.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:14:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.14","text":"न मां कर्माणि लिम्पन्ति न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा ।\nइति मां योऽभिजानाति कर्मभिर्न स बध्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na māṃ karmāṇi limpanti na me karmaphale spṛhā |\niti māṃ yo’bhijānāti karmabhirna sa badhyate ||","body":"Nor do actions affect Me, nor is the fruit of action desired by Me. He who thus knoweth Me is not bound by actions.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","14 of 42"]]},"g2-4-14":{"route":"#/gitav/4.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:14:en2","title":"Gita 4.14, in another translation","body":"Actions do not taint Me, nor have I any thirst for the result of action. He who knows Me thus is not fettered by action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","14 of 42"]]},"gv-4-15":{"route":"#/gitav/4.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:15:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.15","text":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः ।\nकुरु कर्मैव तस्मात्त्वं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरं कृतम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"evaṃ jñātvā kṛtaṃ karma pūrvairapi mumukṣubhiḥ |\nkuru karmaiva tasmāttvaṃ pūrvaiḥ pūrvataraṃ kṛtam ||","body":"Having thus known, our forefathers, ever seeking liberation, performed action; therefore do thou also perform action, as did our forefathers in the olden time.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","15 of 42"]]},"g2-4-15":{"route":"#/gitav/4.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:15:en2","title":"Gita 4.15, in another translation","body":"Knowing thus, the ancient seekers after freedom also performed action. Do thou, therefore, perform action, as did the ancients in olden times.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","15 of 42"]]},"gv-4-16":{"route":"#/gitav/4.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:16:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.16","text":"किं कर्म किमकर्मेति कवयोऽप्यत्र मोहिताः ।\nतत्ते कर्म प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kiṃ karma kimakarmeti kavayo’pyatra mohitāḥ |\ntatte karma pravakṣyāmi yajjñātvā mokṣyase’śubhāt ||","body":"\"What is action, what inaction\"? Even the wise are herein perplexed. Therefore I will declare to thee the action by knowing which thou shalt be loosed from evil.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","16 of 42"]]},"g2-4-16":{"route":"#/gitav/4.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:16:en2","title":"Gita 4.16, in another translation","body":"Even sages are bewildered, as to what is action and what is inaction. I shall therefore tell you what action is, by knowing which you will be freed from evil.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","16 of 42"]]},"gv-4-17":{"route":"#/gitav/4.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:17:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.17","text":"कर्मणो ह्यपि बोद्धव्यं बोद्धव्यं च विकर्मणः ।\nअकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmaṇo hyapi boddhavyaṃ boddhavyaṃ ca vikarmaṇaḥ |\nakarmaṇaśca boddhavyaṃ gahanā karmaṇo gatiḥ ||","body":"It is needful to discriminate action, to discriminate unlawful action, and to discriminate inaction; mysterious is the path of action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","17 of 42"]]},"g2-4-17":{"route":"#/gitav/4.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:17:en2","title":"Gita 4.17, in another translation","body":"For verily, (the true nature) even of action (enjoined by the Shâstras) should be known, as also, (that) of forbidden action, and of inaction: the nature of Karma is impenetrable.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","17 of 42"]]},"gv-4-18":{"route":"#/gitav/4.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:18:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.18","text":"कर्मण्यकर्म यः पश्येदकर्मणि च कर्म यः ।\nस बुद्धिमान् मनुष्येषु स युक्तः कृत्स्नकर्मकृत् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"karmaṇyakarma yaḥ paśyedakarmaṇi ca karma yaḥ |\nsa buddhimān manuṣyeṣu sa yuktaḥ kṛtsnakarmakṛt ||","body":"He who seeth inaction in action, and action in inaction, he is wise among men, he is harmonious, even while performing all action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","18 of 42"]]},"g2-4-18":{"route":"#/gitav/4.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:18:en2","title":"Gita 4.18, in another translation","body":"He who sees inaction in action, and action in inaction, he is intelligent among men, he is a Yogi and a doer of all action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","18 of 42"]]},"gv-4-19":{"route":"#/gitav/4.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:19:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.19","text":"यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः ।\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yasya sarve samārambhāḥ kāmasaṅkalpavarjitāḥ |\njñānāgnidagdhakarmāṇaṃ tamāhuḥ paṇḍitaṃ budhāḥ ||","body":"Whose works are all free from the moulding of desire, whose actions are burned up by the fire of wisdom, him the wise have called a Sage.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","19 of 42"]]},"g2-4-19":{"route":"#/gitav/4.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:19:en2","title":"Gita 4.19, in another translation","body":"Whose undertakings are all devoid of plan and desire for results, and whose actions are burnt by the fire of knowledge, him, the sages call wise.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","19 of 42"]]},"gv-4-20":{"route":"#/gitav/4.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:20:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.20","text":"त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गं नित्यतृप्तो निराश्रयः ।\nकर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किञ्चित्करोति सः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tyaktvā karmaphalāsaṅgaṃ nityatṛpto nirāśrayaḥ |\nkarmaṇyabhipravṛtto’pi naiva kiñcitkaroti saḥ ||","body":"Having abandoned attachment to the fruit of action, always content, nowhere seeking refuge, he is not doing anything, although doing actions.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","20 of 42"]]},"g2-4-20":{"route":"#/gitav/4.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:20:en2","title":"Gita 4.20, in another translation","body":"Forsaking the clinging to fruits of action, ever satisfied, depending on nothing, though engaged in action, he does not do anything.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","20 of 42"]]},"gv-4-21":{"route":"#/gitav/4.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:21:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.21","text":"निराशीर्यतचित्तात्मा त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nशारीरं केवलं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"nirāśīryatacittātmā tyaktasarvaparigrahaḥ |\nśārīraṃ kevalaṃ karma kurvannāpnoti kilbiṣam ||","body":"Hoping for naught, his mind and self controlled, having abandoned all greed, performing action by the body alone, he doth not commit sin.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","21 of 42"]]},"g2-4-21":{"route":"#/gitav/4.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:21:en2","title":"Gita 4.21, in another translation","body":"Without hope, the body and mind controlled and all possessions relinquished, he does not suffer any evil consequences, by doing mere bodily action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","21 of 42"]]},"gv-4-22":{"route":"#/gitav/4.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:22:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.22","text":"यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टो द्वन्द्वातीतो विमत्सरः ।\nसमः सिद्धावसिद्धौ च कृत्वापि न निबध्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadṛcchālābhasantuṣṭo dvandvātīto vimatsaraḥ |\nsamaḥ siddhāvasiddhau ca kṛtvāpi na nibadhyate ||","body":"Content with whatsoever he obtaineth without effort, free from the pairs of opposites, without envy, balanced in success and failure, though acting he is not bound.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","22 of 42"]]},"g2-4-22":{"route":"#/gitav/4.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:22:en2","title":"Gita 4.22, in another translation","body":"Content with what comes to him without effort, unaffected by the pairs of opposites, free from envy, even-minded in success and failure, though acting, he is not bound.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","22 of 42"]]},"gv-4-23":{"route":"#/gitav/4.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:23:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.23","text":"गतसङ्गस्य मुक्तस्य ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः ।\nयज्ञायाचरतः कर्म समग्रं प्रविलीयते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"gatasaṅgasya muktasya jñānāvasthitacetasaḥ |\nyajñāyācarataḥ karma samagraṃ pravilīyate ||","body":"Of one with attachment dead, harmonious, with his thoughts established in wisdom, his works sacrifices, all action melts away.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","23 of 42"]]},"g2-4-23":{"route":"#/gitav/4.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:23:en2","title":"Gita 4.23, in another translation","body":"Devoid of attachment, liberated, with mind centred in knowledge, performing work for Yajna alone, his whole Karma dissolves away.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","23 of 42"]]},"gv-4-24":{"route":"#/gitav/4.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:24:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.24","text":"ब्रह्मार्पणं ब्रह्महविर्ब्रह्माग्नौ ब्रह्मणा हुतम् ।\nब्रह्मैव तेन गन्तव्यं ब्रह्मकर्मसमाधिना ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"brahmārpaṇaṃ brahmahavirbrahmāgnau brahmaṇā hutam |\nbrahmaiva tena gantavyaṃ brahmakarmasamādhinā ||","body":"The Eternal the oblation, the Eternal the clarified butter, are offered in the Eternal the fire by the Eternal; unto the Eternal verily shall he go who in his action meditateth wholly upon the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","24 of 42"]]},"g2-4-24":{"route":"#/gitav/4.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:24:en2","title":"Gita 4.24, in another translation","body":"The process is Brahman, the clarified butter is Brahman, offered by Brahman in the fire of Brahman; by seeing Brahman in action, he reaches Brahman alone.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","24 of 42"]]},"gv-4-25":{"route":"#/gitav/4.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:25:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.25","text":"दैवमेवापरे यज्ञं योगिनः पर्युपासते ।\nब्रह्माग्नावपरे यज्ञं यज्ञेनैवोपजुह्वति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"daivamevāpare yajñaṃ yoginaḥ paryupāsate |\nbrahmāgnāvapare yajñaṃ yajñenaivopajuhvati ||","body":"Some Yogis offer up sacrifice to the Shining Ones; others sacrifice only by pouring sacrifice into the fire of the Eternal;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","25 of 42"]]},"g2-4-25":{"route":"#/gitav/4.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:25:en2","title":"Gita 4.25, in another translation","body":"Some Yogis perform sacrifices to Devas alone, while others offer the self as sacrifice by the self in the fire of Brahman alone.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","25 of 42"]]},"gv-4-26":{"route":"#/gitav/4.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:26:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.26","text":"श्रोत्रादीनीन्द्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयानन्य इन्द्रियाग्निषु जुह्वति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śrotrādīnīndriyāṇyanye saṃyamāgniṣu juhvati |\nśabdādīnviṣayānanya indriyāgniṣu juhvati ||","body":"Some pour as sacrifice hearing and the other senses into the fires of restraint; some pour sound and the other objects of sense into the fires of the senses as sacrifice;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","26 of 42"]]},"g2-4-26":{"route":"#/gitav/4.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:26:en2","title":"Gita 4.26, in another translation","body":"Some again offer hearing and other senses as sacrifice in the fire of control, while others offer sound and other sense-objects as sacrifice in the fire of the senses.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","26 of 42"]]},"gv-4-27":{"route":"#/gitav/4.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:27:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.27","text":"सर्वाणीन्द्रियकर्माणि प्राणकर्माणि चापरे ।\nआत्मसंयमयोगाग्नौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sarvāṇīndriyakarmāṇi prāṇakarmāṇi cāpare |\nātmasaṃyamayogāgnau juhvati jñānadīpite ||","body":"Others again into the wisdom-kindled fire of union attained by self-control, pour as sacrifice all the functions of the senses and the functions of life;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","27 of 42"]]},"g2-4-27":{"route":"#/gitav/4.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:27:en2","title":"Gita 4.27, in another translation","body":"Some again offer all the actions of the senses and the functions of the vital energy, as sacrifice in the fire of control in self, kindled by knowledge.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","27 of 42"]]},"gv-4-28":{"route":"#/gitav/4.28","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:28:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.28","text":"द्रव्ययज्ञास्तपोयज्ञा योगयज्ञास्तथापरे ।\nस्वाध्यायज्ञानयज्ञाश्च यतयः संशितव्रताः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"dravyayajñāstapoyajñā yogayajñāstathāpare |\nsvādhyāyajñānayajñāśca yatayaḥ saṃśitavratāḥ ||","body":"Yet others the sacrifice of wealth, the sacrifice of austerity, the sacrifice of yoga, the sacrifice of silent reading and wisdom, men concentrated and of effectual vows;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","28 of 42"]]},"g2-4-28":{"route":"#/gitav/4.28","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:28:en2","title":"Gita 4.28, in another translation","body":"Others again offer wealth, austerity, and Yoga, as sacrifice, while still others, of self-restraint and rigid vows, offer study of the scriptures and knowledge, as sacrifice.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","28 of 42"]]},"gv-4-29":{"route":"#/gitav/4.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:29:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.29","text":"अपाने जुह्वति प्राणं प्राणेऽपानं तथापरे ।\nप्राणापानगती रुद्ध्वा प्राणायामपरायणाः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"apāne juhvati prāṇaṃ prāṇe’pānaṃ tathāpare |\nprāṇāpānagatī ruddhvā prāṇāyāmaparāyaṇāḥ ||","body":"Yet others pour as sacrifice the outgoing breath in the incoming, and the incoming in the outgoing, restraining the flow of the outgoing and incoming breaths, solely absorbed in the control of breathing.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","29 of 42"]]},"g2-4-29":{"route":"#/gitav/4.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:29:en2","title":"Gita 4.29, in another translation","body":"Yet some offer as sacrifice, the outgoing into the in-coming breath, and the in-coming into the out-going, stopping the courses of the in-coming and out-going breaths, constantly practising the regulation of the vital energy; while others yet of regulated food, offer in the Prânas the functions thereof.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","29 of 42"]]},"gv-4-30":{"route":"#/gitav/4.30","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:30:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.30","text":"अपरे नियताहाराः प्राणान्प्राणेषु जुह्वति ।\nसर्वेऽप्येते यज्ञविदो यज्ञक्षपितकल्मषाः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"apare niyatāhārāḥ prāṇānprāṇeṣu juhvati |\nsarve’pyete yajñavido yajñakṣapitakalmaṣāḥ ||","body":"Others regular in food, pour as sacrifice their life-breaths in life-breaths. All these are knowers of sacrifice, and by sacrifice have destroyed their sins.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","30 of 42"]]},"g2-4-30":{"route":"#/gitav/4.30","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:30:en2","title":"Gita 4.30, in another translation","body":"All of these are knowers of Yajna, having their sins consumed by Yajna, and eating of the nectar—the remnant of Yajna, they go to the Eternal Brahman. (Even) this world is not for the non-performer of Yajna, how then another, O best of the Kurus?","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","30 of 42"]]},"gv-4-31":{"route":"#/gitav/4.31","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:31:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.31","text":"यज्ञशिष्टामृतभुजो यान्ति ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञस्य कुतोऽन्यः कुरुसत्तम ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yajñaśiṣṭāmṛtabhujo yānti brahma sanātanam |\nnāyaṃ loko’styayajñasya kuto’nyaḥ kurusattama ||","body":"The eaters of the life-giving remains of sacrifice go to the changeless Eternal. This world is not for the non-sacrificer, much less the other, O best of the Kurus.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","31 of 42"]]},"gv-4-32":{"route":"#/gitav/4.32","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:32:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.32","text":"एवं बहुविधा यज्ञा वितता ब्रह्मणो मुखे ।\nकर्मजान्विद्धि तान्सर्वानेवं ज्ञात्वा विमोक्ष्यसे ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"evaṃ bahuvidhā yajñā vitatā brahmaṇo mukhe |\nkarmajānviddhi tānsarvānevaṃ jñātvā vimokṣyase ||","body":"Many and various sacrifices are thus spread out before the Eternal. Know thou that all these are born of action, and thus knowing thou shalt be free.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","32 of 42"]]},"g2-4-32":{"route":"#/gitav/4.32","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:32:en2","title":"Gita 4.32, in another translation","body":"Various Yajnas, like the above, are strewn in the store-house of the Veda. Know them all to be born of action, and thus knowing, thou shalt be free.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","32 of 42"]]},"gv-4-33":{"route":"#/gitav/4.33","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:33:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.33","text":"श्रेयान्द्रव्यमयाद्यज्ञाज्ज्ञानयज्ञः परन्तप ।\nसर्वं कर्माखिलं पार्थ ज्ञाने परिसमाप्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śreyāndravyamayādyajñājjñānayajñaḥ parantapa |\nsarvaṃ karmākhilaṃ pārtha jñāne parisamāpyate ||","body":"Better than the sacrifice of any objects is the sacrifice of wisdom, O Parantapa. All actions in their entirety, O Pârtha, culminate in wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","33 of 42"]]},"g2-4-33":{"route":"#/gitav/4.33","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:33:en2","title":"Gita 4.33, in another translation","body":"Knowledge-sacrifice, O scorcher of foes, is superior to sacrifice (performed) with (material) objects. All action in its entirety, O Pârtha, attains its consummation in knowledge.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","33 of 42"]]},"gv-4-34":{"route":"#/gitav/4.34","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:34:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.34","text":"तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया ।\nउपदेक्ष्यन्ति ते ज्ञानं ज्ञानिनस्तत्त्वदर्शिनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tadviddhi praṇipātena paripraśnena sevayā |\nupadekṣyanti te jñānaṃ jñāninastattvadarśinaḥ ||","body":"Learn thou this by discipleship, by investiga tion, and by service. The wise, the seers of the essence of things, will instruct thee in wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","34 of 42"]]},"g2-4-34":{"route":"#/gitav/4.34","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:34:en2","title":"Gita 4.34, in another translation","body":"Know that, by prostrating thyself, by questions, and by service; the wise, those who have realised the Truth, will instruct thee in that knowledge.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","34 of 42"]]},"gv-4-35":{"route":"#/gitav/4.35","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:35:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.35","text":"यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं यास्यसि पाण्डव ।\nयेन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yajjñātvā na punarmohamevaṃ yāsyasi pāṇḍava |\nyena bhūtānyaśeṣeṇa drakṣyasyātmanyatho mayi ||","body":"And having known this, thou shalt not again fall into this confusion, O Pândava; for by this thou wilt see all beings without exception in the Self, and thus in Me.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","35 of 42"]]},"g2-4-35":{"route":"#/gitav/4.35","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:35:en2","title":"Gita 4.35, in another translation","body":"Knowing which, thou shalt not, O Pândava, again get deluded like this, and by which thou shalt see the whole of creation in (thy) Self and in Me.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","35 of 42"]]},"gv-4-36":{"route":"#/gitav/4.36","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:36:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.36","text":"अपि चेदसि पापेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः पापकृत्तमः ।\nसर्वं ज्ञानप्लवेनैव वृजिनं सन्तरिष्यसि ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"api cedasi pāpebhyaḥ sarvebhyaḥ pāpakṛttamaḥ |\nsarvaṃ jñānaplavenaiva vṛjinaṃ santariṣyasi ||","body":"Even if thou art the most sinful of all sinners, yet shalt thou cross over all sin by the raft of wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","36 of 42"]]},"g2-4-36":{"route":"#/gitav/4.36","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:36:en2","title":"Gita 4.36, in another translation","body":"Even if thou be the most sinful among all the sinful, yet by the raft of knowledge alone thou shalt go across all sin.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","36 of 42"]]},"gv-4-37":{"route":"#/gitav/4.37","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:37:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.37","text":"यथैधांसि समिद्धोऽग्निर्भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुते तथा ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yathaidhāṃsi samiddho’gnirbhasmasātkurute’rjuna |\njñānāgniḥ sarvakarmāṇi bhasmasātkurute tathā ||","body":"As the burning fire reduces fuel to ashes, O Arjuna, so doth the fire of wisdom reduce all actions to ashes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","37 of 42"]]},"g2-4-37":{"route":"#/gitav/4.37","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:37:en2","title":"Gita 4.37, in another translation","body":"As blazing fire reduces wood into ashes, so, O Arjuna, does the fire of knowledge reduce all Karma to ashes.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","37 of 42"]]},"gv-4-38":{"route":"#/gitav/4.38","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:38:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.38","text":"न हि ज्ञानेन सदृशं पवित्रमिह विद्यते ।\nतत्स्वयं योगसंसिद्धः कालेनात्मनि विन्दति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na hi jñānena sadṛśaṃ pavitramiha vidyate |\ntatsvayaṃ yogasaṃsiddhaḥ kālenātmani vindati ||","body":"Verily there is no purifier in this world like wisdom; he that is perfected in yoga finds it in the Self in due season.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","38 of 42"]]},"g2-4-38":{"route":"#/gitav/4.38","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:38:en2","title":"Gita 4.38, in another translation","body":"Verily there exists nothing in this world purifying like knowledge. In good time, having reached perfection in Yoga, one realises that oneself in one's own heart.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","38 of 42"]]},"gv-4-39":{"route":"#/gitav/4.39","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:39:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.39","text":"श्रद्धावाँल्लभते ज्ञानं तत्परः संयतेन्द्रियः ।\nज्ञानं लब्ध्वा परां शान्तिमचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śraddhāvām̐llabhate jñānaṃ tatparaḥ saṃyatendriyaḥ |\njñānaṃ labdhvā parāṃ śāntimacireṇādhigacchati ||","body":"The man who is full of faith obtaineth wisdom, and he also who hath mastery over his senses; and, having obtained wisdom, he goeth swiftly to the supreme Peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","39 of 42"]]},"g2-4-39":{"route":"#/gitav/4.39","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:39:en2","title":"Gita 4.39, in another translation","body":"The man with Shraddhâ, the devoted, the master of one's senses, attains (this) knowledge. Having attained knowledge one goes at once to the Supreme Peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","39 of 42"]]},"gv-4-40":{"route":"#/gitav/4.40","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:40:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.40","text":"अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च संशयात्मा विनश्यति ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्ति न परो न सुखं संशयात्मनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ajñaścāśraddadhānaśca saṃśayātmā vinaśyati |\nnāyaṃ loko’sti na paro na sukhaṃ saṃśayātmanaḥ ||","body":"But the ignorant, faithless, doubting self goeth to destruction; nor this world, nor that beyond, nor happiness, is there for the doubting self.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","40 of 42"]]},"g2-4-40":{"route":"#/gitav/4.40","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:40:en2","title":"Gita 4.40, in another translation","body":"The ignorant, the man without Shraddhâ, the doubting self, goes to destruction. The doubting self has neither this world, nor the next, nor happiness.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","40 of 42"]]},"gv-4-41":{"route":"#/gitav/4.41","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:41:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.41","text":"योगसंन्यस्तकर्माणं ज्ञानसंछिन्नसंशयम् ।\nआत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yogasaṃnyastakarmāṇaṃ jñānasaṃchinnasaṃśayam |\nātmavantaṃ na karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya ||","body":"He who hath renounced actions by yoga, who hath cloven asunder doubt by wisdom, who is ruled by the Self, actions do not bind him, O Dhananjaya.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","41 of 42"]]},"g2-4-41":{"route":"#/gitav/4.41","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:41:en2","title":"Gita 4.41, in another translation","body":"With work renounced by Yoga and doubts rent asunder by knowledge, O Dhananjaya, actions do not bind him who is poised in the Self.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","41 of 42"]]},"gv-4-42":{"route":"#/gitav/4.42","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:42:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 4.42","text":"तस्मादज्ञानसंभूतं हृत्स्थं ज्ञानासिनाऽऽत्मनः ।\nछित्त्वैनं संशयं योगमातिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ भारत ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tasmādajñānasaṃbhūtaṃ hṛtsthaṃ jñānāsinā’’tmanaḥ |\nchittvainaṃ saṃśayaṃ yogamātiṣṭhottiṣṭha bhārata ||","body":"Therefore, with the sword of the wisdom of the Self cleaving asunder this ignorance-born doubt dwelling in thy heart, be established in yoga. Stand up, O Bhârata.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","42 of 42"]]},"g2-4-42":{"route":"#/gitav/4.42","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 4 — The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge","src":"gita:4:42:en2","title":"Gita 4.42, in another translation","body":"Therefore, cutting with the sword of knowledge, this doubt about the Self, born of ignorance, residing in thy heart, take refuge in Yoga. Arise, O Bhârata!","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation of Action in Knowledge"],["Verse","42 of 42"]]},"gv-5-1":{"route":"#/gitav/5.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:1:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.1","text":"संन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि ।\nयच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्चितम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"saṃnyāsaṃ karmaṇāṃ kṛṣṇa punaryogaṃ ca śaṃsasi |\nyacchreya etayorekaṃ tanme brūhi suniścitam ||","body":"Arjuna said: Renunciation of actions Thou praisest, O Krishna, and then also yoga. Of the two which one is the better? That tell me conclusively.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","1 of 29"]]},"g2-5-1":{"route":"#/gitav/5.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:1:en2","title":"Gita 5.1, in another translation","body":"Renunciation of action, O Krishna, thou commendest, and again, its performance. Which is the better one of these? Do thou tell me decisively.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","1 of 29"]]},"gv-5-2":{"route":"#/gitav/5.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:2:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.2","text":"संन्यासः कर्मयोगश्च निःश्रेयसकरावुभौ ।\nतयोस्तु कर्मसंन्यासात्कर्मयोगो विशिष्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"saṃnyāsaḥ karmayogaśca niḥśreyasakarāvubhau |\ntayostu karmasaṃnyāsātkarmayogo viśiṣyate ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: Renunciation and yoga by action both lead to the highest bliss; of the two, yoga by action is verily better than renunciation of action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","2 of 29"]]},"g2-5-2":{"route":"#/gitav/5.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:2:en2","title":"Gita 5.2, in another translation","body":"Both renunciation and performance of action lead to freedom: of these, performance of action is superior to the renunciation of action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","2 of 29"]]},"gv-5-3":{"route":"#/gitav/5.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:3:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.3","text":"ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी यो न द्वेष्टि न काङ्क्षति ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो हि महाबाहो सुखं बन्धात्प्रमुच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"jñeyaḥ sa nityasaṃnyāsī yo na dveṣṭi na kāṅkṣati |\nnirdvandvo hi mahābāho sukhaṃ bandhātpramucyate ||","body":"He should be known as a perpetual ascetic, who neither hateth nor desireth; free from the pairs of opposites, O mighty-armed, he is easily set free from bondage.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","3 of 29"]]},"g2-5-3":{"route":"#/gitav/5.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:3:en2","title":"Gita 5.3, in another translation","body":"He should be known a constant Sannyâsi, who neither likes nor dislikes: for, free from the pairs of opposites, mighty-armed, he is easily set free from bondage.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","3 of 29"]]},"gv-5-4":{"route":"#/gitav/5.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:4:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.4","text":"सांख्ययोगौ पृथग्बालाः प्रवदन्ति न पण्डिताः ।\nएकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते फलम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sāṃkhyayogau pṛthagbālāḥ pravadanti na paṇḍitāḥ |\nekamapyāsthitaḥ samyagubhayorvindate phalam ||","body":"Children, not sages, speak of the Sânkhya and the Yoga as different; he who is duly established in one obtaineth the fruits of both.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","4 of 29"]]},"g2-5-4":{"route":"#/gitav/5.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:4:en2","title":"Gita 5.4, in another translation","body":"Children, not the wise, speak of knowledge and performance of action, as distinct. He who truly lives in one, gains the fruits of both.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","4 of 29"]]},"gv-5-5":{"route":"#/gitav/5.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:5:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.5","text":"यत्सांख्यैः प्राप्यते स्थानं तद्योगैरपि गम्यते ।\nएकं सांख्यं च योगं च यः पश्यति स पश्यति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yatsāṃkhyaiḥ prāpyate sthānaṃ tadyogairapi gamyate |\nekaṃ sāṃkhyaṃ ca yogaṃ ca yaḥ paśyati sa paśyati ||","body":"That place which is gained by the Sânkhyas is reached by the Yogîs also. He seeth, who seeth that the Sânkhya and the Yoga are one.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","5 of 29"]]},"g2-5-5":{"route":"#/gitav/5.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:5:en2","title":"Gita 5.5, in another translation","body":"The plane which is reached by the Jnânins is also reached by the Karmayogins. Who sees knowledge and performance of action as one, he sees.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","5 of 29"]]},"gv-5-6":{"route":"#/gitav/5.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:6:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.6","text":"संन्यासस्तु महाबाहो दुःखमाप्तुमयोगतः ।\nयोगयुक्तो मुनिर्ब्रह्म नचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"saṃnyāsastu mahābāho duḥkhamāptumayogataḥ |\nyogayukto munirbrahma nacireṇādhigacchati ||","body":"But without yoga, O mighty-armed, renunciation is hard to attain to; the yoga-harmonised Muni swiftly goeth to the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","6 of 29"]]},"g2-5-6":{"route":"#/gitav/5.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:6:en2","title":"Gita 5.6, in another translation","body":"Renunciation of action, O mighty-armed, is hard to attain to without performance of action; the man of meditation, purified by devotion to action, quickly goes to Brahman.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","6 of 29"]]},"gv-5-7":{"route":"#/gitav/5.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:7:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.7","text":"योगयुक्तो विशुद्धात्मा विजितात्मा जितेन्द्रियः ।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतात्मा कुर्वन्नपि न लिप्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yogayukto viśuddhātmā vijitātmā jitendriyaḥ |\nsarvabhūtātmabhūtātmā kurvannapi na lipyate ||","body":"He who is harmonised by yoga, the self purified, Self -ruled, the senses subdued, whose Self is the Self of all beings, although acting he is not affected.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","7 of 29"]]},"g2-5-7":{"route":"#/gitav/5.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:7:en2","title":"Gita 5.7, in another translation","body":"With the mind purified by devotion to performance of action, and the body conquered, and senses subdued, one who realises one's Self, as the Self in all beings, though acting, is not tainted.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","7 of 29"]]},"gv-5-8":{"route":"#/gitav/5.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:8:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.8","text":"नैव किञ्चित्करोमीति युक्तो मन्येत तत्त्ववित् ।\nपश्यञ्शृण्वन्स्पृशञ्जिघ्रन्नश्नन्गच्छन्स्वपञ्श्वसन् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"naiva kiñcitkaromīti yukto manyeta tattvavit |\npaśyañśṛṇvanspṛśañjighrannaśnangacchansvapañśvasan ||","body":"\"I do not anything,\" should think the harmonised one, who knoweth the essence of things; seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, moving, sleeping, breathing.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","8 of 29"]]},"g2-5-8":{"route":"#/gitav/5.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:8:en2","title":"Gita 5.8, in another translation","body":"The knower of Truth, (being) centred (in the Self) should think, \"I do nothing at all\"—though seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, going, sleeping, breathing, speaking, letting go, holding, opening and closing the eyes—convinced that it is the senses that move among sense-objects.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","8 of 29"]]},"gv-5-9":{"route":"#/gitav/5.9","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:9:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.9","text":"प्रलपन्विसृजन्गृह्णन्नुन्मिषन्निमिषन्नपि ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेषु वर्तन्त इति धारयन् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"pralapanvisṛjangṛhṇannunmiṣannimiṣannapi |\nindriyāṇīndriyārtheṣu vartanta iti dhārayan ||","body":"Speaking, giving, grasping, opening and closing the eyes, he holdeth: \"The senses move among the objects of the senses.\"","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","9 of 29"]]},"gv-5-10":{"route":"#/gitav/5.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:10:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.10","text":"ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा करोति यः ।\nलिप्यते न स पापेन पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"brahmaṇyādhāya karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā karoti yaḥ |\nlipyate na sa pāpena padmapatramivāmbhasā ||","body":"He who acteth, placing all actions in the Eternal, abandoning attachment, is unaffected by sin as a lotus leaf by the waters.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","10 of 29"]]},"g2-5-10":{"route":"#/gitav/5.10","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:10:en2","title":"Gita 5.10, in another translation","body":"He who does actions forsaking attachment, resigning them to Brahman, is not soiled by evil, like unto a lotus-leaf by water.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","10 of 29"]]},"gv-5-11":{"route":"#/gitav/5.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:11:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.11","text":"कायेन मनसा बुद्ध्या केवलैरिन्द्रियैरपि ।\nयोगिनः कर्म कुर्वन्ति सङ्गं त्यक्त्वाऽऽत्मशुद्धये ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kāyena manasā buddhyā kevalairindriyairapi |\nyoginaḥ karma kurvanti saṅgaṃ tyaktvā’’tmaśuddhaye ||","body":"Yogis, having abandoned attachment, perform action only by the body, by the mind, by the Reason, and even by the senses, for the purification of the self.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","11 of 29"]]},"g2-5-11":{"route":"#/gitav/5.11","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:11:en2","title":"Gita 5.11, in another translation","body":"Devotees in the path of work perform action, only with body, mind, senses, and intellect, forsaking attachment, for the purification of the heart.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","11 of 29"]]},"gv-5-12":{"route":"#/gitav/5.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:12:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.12","text":"युक्तः कर्मफलं त्यक्त्वा शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् ।\nअयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yuktaḥ karmaphalaṃ tyaktvā śāntimāpnoti naiṣṭhikīm |\nayuktaḥ kāmakāreṇa phale sakto nibadhyate ||","body":"The harmonised man, having abandoned the fruit of action, attaineth to the eternal Peace; the non-harmonised, impelled by desire, attached to fruit, are bound.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","12 of 29"]]},"g2-5-12":{"route":"#/gitav/5.12","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:12:en2","title":"Gita 5.12, in another translation","body":"The well-poised, forsaking the fruit of action, attains peace, born of steadfastness; the unbalanced one, led by desire, is bound by being attached to the fruit (of action).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","12 of 29"]]},"gv-5-13":{"route":"#/gitav/5.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:13:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.13","text":"सर्वकर्माणि मनसा संन्यस्यास्ते सुखं वशी ।\nनवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन्न कारयन् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sarvakarmāṇi manasā saṃnyasyāste sukhaṃ vaśī |\nnavadvāre pure dehī naiva kurvanna kārayan ||","body":"Mentally renouncing all actions, the sovereign dweller in the body resteth serenely in the nine-gated city, neither acting nor causing to act.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","13 of 29"]]},"g2-5-13":{"route":"#/gitav/5.13","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:13:en2","title":"Gita 5.13, in another translation","body":"The subduer (of the senses), having renounced all actions by discrimination, rests happily in the city of the nine gates, neither acting, nor causing (others) to act.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","13 of 29"]]},"gv-5-14":{"route":"#/gitav/5.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:14:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.14","text":"न कर्तृत्वं न कर्माणि लोकस्य सृजति प्रभुः ।\nन कर्मफलसंयोगं स्वभावस्तु प्रवर्तते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na kartṛtvaṃ na karmāṇi lokasya sṛjati prabhuḥ |\nna karmaphalasaṃyogaṃ svabhāvastu pravartate ||","body":"The Lord of the world produceth not the idea of agency, nor actions, nor the union together of action and its fruit; nature, however, manifesteth.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","14 of 29"]]},"g2-5-14":{"route":"#/gitav/5.14","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:14:en2","title":"Gita 5.14, in another translation","body":"Neither agency, nor actions does the Lord create for the world, nor (does He bring about) the union with the fruit of action. It is universal ignorance that does. (it all).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","14 of 29"]]},"gv-5-15":{"route":"#/gitav/5.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:15:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.15","text":"नादत्ते कस्यचित्पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः ।\nअज्ञानेनावृतं ज्ञानं तेन मुह्यन्ति जन्तवः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"nādatte kasyacitpāpaṃ na caiva sukṛtaṃ vibhuḥ |\najñānenāvṛtaṃ jñānaṃ tena muhyanti jantavaḥ ||","body":"The Lord accepteth neither the evil-doing nor yet the well-doing of any. Wisdom is enveloped by unwisdom; therewith mortals are deluded.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","15 of 29"]]},"g2-5-15":{"route":"#/gitav/5.15","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:15:en2","title":"Gita 5.15, in another translation","body":"The Omnipresent takes note of the merit or demerit of none. Knowledge is enveloped in ignorance, hence do beings get deluded.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","15 of 29"]]},"gv-5-16":{"route":"#/gitav/5.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:16:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.16","text":"ज्ञानेन तु तदज्ञानं येषां नाशितमात्मनः ।\nतेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत्परम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"jñānena tu tadajñānaṃ yeṣāṃ nāśitamātmanaḥ |\nteṣāmādityavajjñānaṃ prakāśayati tatparam ||","body":"Verily, in whom unwisdom is destroyed by the wisdom of the Self, in them wisdom, shining as the sun, reveals the Supreme.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","16 of 29"]]},"g2-5-16":{"route":"#/gitav/5.16","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:16:en2","title":"Gita 5.16, in another translation","body":"But whose ignorance is destroyed by the knowledge of Self,—that knowledge of theirs, like the sun, reveals the Supreme (Brahman).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","16 of 29"]]},"gv-5-17":{"route":"#/gitav/5.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:17:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.17","text":"तद्बुद्धयस्तदात्मानस्तन्निष्ठास्तत्परायणाः ।\nगच्छन्त्यपुनरावृत्तिं ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"tadbuddhayastadātmānastanniṣṭhāstatparāyaṇāḥ |\ngacchantyapunarāvṛttiṃ jñānanirdhūtakalmaṣāḥ ||","body":"Thinking on That, merged in That, established in That, solely devoted to That, they go whence there is no return, their sins dispelled by wisdom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","17 of 29"]]},"g2-5-17":{"route":"#/gitav/5.17","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:17:en2","title":"Gita 5.17, in another translation","body":"Those who have their intellect absorbed in That, whose self is That, whose steadfastness is in That, whose consummation is That, their impurities cleansed by knowledge, they attain to Non-return (Moksha).","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","17 of 29"]]},"gv-5-18":{"route":"#/gitav/5.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:18:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.18","text":"विद्याविनयसंपन्ने ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि ।\nशुनि चैव श्वपाके च पण्डिताः समदर्शिनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"vidyāvinayasaṃpanne brāhmaṇe gavi hastini |\nśuni caiva śvapāke ca paṇḍitāḥ samadarśinaḥ ||","body":"Sages look equally on a Brâhmana adorned with learning and humility, a cow, an elephant, and even a dog and an outcaste.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","18 of 29"]]},"g2-5-18":{"route":"#/gitav/5.18","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:18:en2","title":"Gita 5.18, in another translation","body":"The knowers of the Self look with an equal eye on a Brâhmana endowed with learning and humility, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and a pariah.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","18 of 29"]]},"gv-5-19":{"route":"#/gitav/5.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:19:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.19","text":"इहैव तैर्जितः सर्गो येषां साम्ये स्थितं मनः ।\nनिर्दोषं हि समं ब्रह्म तस्माद्ब्रह्मणि ते स्थिताः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ihaiva tairjitaḥ sargo yeṣāṃ sāmye sthitaṃ manaḥ |\nnirdoṣaṃ hi samaṃ brahma tasmādbrahmaṇi te sthitāḥ ||","body":"Even here on earth everything is overcome by those whose mind remains balanced; the Eternal is incorruptible and balanced; therefore they are established in the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","19 of 29"]]},"g2-5-19":{"route":"#/gitav/5.19","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:19:en2","title":"Gita 5.19, in another translation","body":"(Relative) existence has been conquered by them, even in this world, whose mind rests in evenness, since Brahman is even and without imperfection: therefore they indeed rest in Brahman.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","19 of 29"]]},"gv-5-20":{"route":"#/gitav/5.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:20:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.20","text":"न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम् ।\nस्थिरबुद्धिरसम्मूढो ब्रह्मविद्ब्रह्मणि स्थितः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"na prahṛṣyetpriyaṃ prāpya nodvijetprāpya cāpriyam |\nsthirabuddhirasammūḍho brahmavidbrahmaṇi sthitaḥ ||","body":"With Reason firm, unperplexed, the knower of the Eternal established in the Eternal, neither rejoiceth on obtaining what is pleasant, nor sorroweth on obtaining what is unpleasant.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","20 of 29"]]},"g2-5-20":{"route":"#/gitav/5.20","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:20:en2","title":"Gita 5.20, in another translation","body":"Resting in Brahman, with intellect steady, and without delusion, the knower of Brahman neither rejoiceth on receiving what is pleasant, nor grieveth on receiving what is unpleasant.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","20 of 29"]]},"gv-5-21":{"route":"#/gitav/5.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:21:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.21","text":"बाह्यस्पर्शेष्वसक्तात्मा विन्दत्यात्मनि यत्सुखम् ।\nस ब्रह्मयोगयुक्तात्मा सुखमक्षयमश्नुते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"bāhyasparśeṣvasaktātmā vindatyātmani yatsukham |\nsa brahmayogayuktātmā sukhamakṣayamaśnute ||","body":"He, whose self is unattached to external contacts and findeth joy in the Self, having the self harmonised with the Eternal by yoga, enjoys imperishable bliss.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","21 of 29"]]},"g2-5-21":{"route":"#/gitav/5.21","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:21:en2","title":"Gita 5.21, in another translation","body":"With the heart unattached to external objects, he realises the joy that is in the Self. With the heart devoted to the meditation of Brahman, he attains un-decaying happiness.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","21 of 29"]]},"gv-5-22":{"route":"#/gitav/5.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:22:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.22","text":"ये हि संस्पर्शजा भोगा दुःखयोनय एव ते ।\nआद्यन्तवन्तः कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुधः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ye hi saṃsparśajā bhogā duḥkhayonaya eva te |\nādyantavantaḥ kaunteya na teṣu ramate budhaḥ ||","body":"The delights that are contact-born, they are verily wombs of pain, for they have beginning and ending, O Kaunteya; not in them may rejoice the wise.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","22 of 29"]]},"g2-5-22":{"route":"#/gitav/5.22","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:22:en2","title":"Gita 5.22, in another translation","body":"Since enjoyments that are contact-born are parents of misery alone, and with beginning and end, O son of Kunti, a wise man does not seek pleasure in them.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","22 of 29"]]},"gv-5-23":{"route":"#/gitav/5.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:23:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.23","text":"शक्नोतीहैव यः सोढुं प्राक्शरीरविमोक्षणात् ।\nकामक्रोधोद्भवं वेगं स युक्तः स सुखी नरः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"śaknotīhaiva yaḥ soḍhuṃ prākśarīravimokṣaṇāt |\nkāmakrodhodbhavaṃ vegaṃ sa yuktaḥ sa sukhī naraḥ ||","body":"He who is able to endure here on earth, ere he be liberated from the body, the force born from desire and passion, he is harmonised, he is a happy man.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","23 of 29"]]},"g2-5-23":{"route":"#/gitav/5.23","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:23:en2","title":"Gita 5.23, in another translation","body":"He who can withstand in this world, before the liberation from the body, the impulse arising from lust and anger, he is steadfast (in Yoga), he is a happy man.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","23 of 29"]]},"gv-5-24":{"route":"#/gitav/5.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:24:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.24","text":"योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव यः ।\nस योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yo’ntaḥsukho’ntarārāmastathāntarjyotireva yaḥ |\nsa yogī brahmanirvāṇaṃ brahmabhūto’dhigacchati ||","body":"He who is happy within, who rejoiceth within, who is illuminated within, that Yogî, becoming the Eternal, goeth to the Peace of the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","24 of 29"]]},"g2-5-24":{"route":"#/gitav/5.24","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:24:en2","title":"Gita 5.24, in another translation","body":"Whose happiness is within, whose relaxation is within, whose light is within, that Yogi alone, becoming Brahman, gains absolute freedom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","24 of 29"]]},"gv-5-25":{"route":"#/gitav/5.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:25:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.25","text":"लभन्ते ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृषयः क्षीणकल्मषाः ।\nछिन्नद्वैधा यतात्मानः सर्वभूतहिते रताः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"labhante brahmanirvāṇamṛṣayaḥ kṣīṇakalmaṣāḥ |\nchinnadvaidhā yatātmānaḥ sarvabhūtahite ratāḥ ||","body":"Rishis, their sins destroyed, their duality removed, their selves controlled, intent upon the welfare of all beings, obtain the Peace of the Eternal.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","25 of 29"]]},"g2-5-25":{"route":"#/gitav/5.25","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:25:en2","title":"Gita 5.25, in another translation","body":"With imperfections exhausted, doubts dispelled, senses controlled, engaged in the good of all beings, the Rishis obtain absolute freedom.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","25 of 29"]]},"gv-5-26":{"route":"#/gitav/5.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:26:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.26","text":"कामक्रोधवियुक्तानां यतीनां यतचेतसाम् ।\nअभितो ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं वर्तते विदितात्मनाम् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"kāmakrodhaviyuktānāṃ yatīnāṃ yatacetasām |\nabhito brahmanirvāṇaṃ vartate viditātmanām ||","body":"The Peace of the Eternal lies near to those who know themselves, who are disjoined from desire and passion, subdued in nature, of subdued thoughts.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","26 of 29"]]},"g2-5-26":{"route":"#/gitav/5.26","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:26:en2","title":"Gita 5.26, in another translation","body":"Released from lust and anger, the heart controlled, the Self realised, absolute freedom is for such Sannyâsis, both here and hereafter.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","26 of 29"]]},"gv-5-27":{"route":"#/gitav/5.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:27:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.27","text":"स्पर्शान्कृत्वा बहिर्बाह्यांश्चक्षुश्चैवान्तरे भ्रुवोः ।\nप्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"sparśānkṛtvā bahirbāhyāṃścakṣuścaivāntare bhruvoḥ |\nprāṇāpānau samau kṛtvā nāsābhyantaracāriṇau ||","body":"Having external contacts excluded, and with gaze fixed between the eyebrows; having made equal the outgoing and ingoing breaths moving within the nostrils;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","27 of 29"]]},"g2-5-27":{"route":"#/gitav/5.27","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:27:en2","title":"Gita 5.27, in another translation","body":"Shutting out external objects, steadying the eyes between the eyebrows, restricting the even currents of Prâna and Apâna inside the nostrils; the senses, mind, and intellect controlled, with Moksha as the supreme goal, freed from desire, fear and anger: such a man of meditation is verily free for ever.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","27 of 29"]]},"gv-5-28":{"route":"#/gitav/5.28","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:28:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.28","text":"यतेन्द्रियमनोबुद्धिर्मुनिर्मोक्षपरायणः ।\nविगतेच्छाभयक्रोधो यः सदा मुक्त एव सः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yatendriyamanobuddhirmunirmokṣaparāyaṇaḥ |\nvigatecchābhayakrodho yaḥ sadā mukta eva saḥ ||","body":"With senses, mind, and Reason ever controlled, solely pursuing liberation, the Sage, having for ever cast away desire, fear and passion, verily is liberated.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","28 of 29"]]},"gv-5-29":{"route":"#/gitav/5.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:29:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 5.29","text":"भोक्तारं यज्ञतपसां सर्वलोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nसुहृदं सर्वभूतानां ज्ञात्वा मां शान्तिमृच्छति ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"bhoktāraṃ yajñatapasāṃ sarvalokamaheśvaram |\nsuhṛdaṃ sarvabhūtānāṃ jñātvā māṃ śāntimṛcchati ||","body":"Having known Me, as the Enjoyer of sacrifice and of austerity, the mighty Ruler of all the worlds, and the Lover of all beings, he goeth to Peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","29 of 29"]]},"g2-5-29":{"route":"#/gitav/5.29","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 5 — The Way of Renunciation","src":"gita:5:29:en2","title":"Gita 5.29, in another translation","body":"Knowing Me as the dispenser of Yajnas and asceticisms, as the Great Lord of all worlds, as the friend of all beings, he attains Peace.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Renunciation"],["Verse","29 of 29"]]},"gv-6-1":{"route":"#/gitav/6.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:1:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.1","text":"अनाश्रितः कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति यः ।\nस संन्यासी च योगी च न निरग्निर्न चाक्रियः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"anāśritaḥ karmaphalaṃ kāryaṃ karma karoti yaḥ |\nsa saṃnyāsī ca yogī ca na niragnirna cākriyaḥ ||","body":"The Blessed Lord said: He that performeth such action as his duty, independently of the fruit of action, he is an ascetic, he is a Yogî, not he that is without fire, and without rites.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","1 of 47"]]},"g2-6-1":{"route":"#/gitav/6.1","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:1:en2","title":"Gita 6.1, in another translation","body":"He who performs his bounden duty without leaning to the fruit of action —he is a renouncer of action as well as of steadfast mind: not he who is without fire, nor he who is without action.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","1 of 47"]]},"gv-6-2":{"route":"#/gitav/6.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:2:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.2","text":"यं संन्यासमिति प्राहुर्योगं तं विद्धि पाण्डव ।\nन ह्यसंन्यस्तसङ्कल्पो योगी भवति कश्चन ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yaṃ saṃnyāsamiti prāhuryogaṃ taṃ viddhi pāṇḍava |\nna hyasaṃnyastasaṅkalpo yogī bhavati kaścana ||","body":"That which is called renunciation, know thou that as yoga, O Pândava; nor doth any one become a Yogî with the formative will unrenounced.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","2 of 47"]]},"g2-6-2":{"route":"#/gitav/6.2","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:2:en2","title":"Gita 6.2, in another translation","body":"Know that to be devotion to action, which is called renunciation, O Pândava, for none becomes a devotee to action without forsaking Sankalpa.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","2 of 47"]]},"gv-6-3":{"route":"#/gitav/6.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:3:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.3","text":"आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगं कर्म कारणमुच्यते ।\nयोगारूढस्य तस्यैव शमः कारणमुच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"ārurukṣormuneryogaṃ karma kāraṇamucyate |\nyogārūḍhasya tasyaiva śamaḥ kāraṇamucyate ||","body":"For a Sage who is seeking Yoga, action is called the means; for the same Sage, when he is enthroned in yoga, serenity is called the means.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","3 of 47"]]},"g2-6-3":{"route":"#/gitav/6.3","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:3:en2","title":"Gita 6.3, in another translation","body":"For the man of meditation wishing to attain purification of heart leading to concentration, work is said to be the way: For him, when he has attained such (concentration), inaction is said to be the way.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","3 of 47"]]},"gv-6-4":{"route":"#/gitav/6.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:4:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.4","text":"यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते ।\nसर्वसङ्कल्पसंन्यासी योगारूढस्तदोच्यते ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"yadā hi nendriyārtheṣu na karmasvanuṣajjate |\nsarvasaṅkalpasaṃnyāsī yogārūḍhastadocyate ||","body":"When a man feeleth no attachment either for the objects of sense or for actions, renouncing the formative will, then, he is said to be enthroned in yoga.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","4 of 47"]]},"g2-6-4":{"route":"#/gitav/6.4","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:4:en2","title":"Gita 6.4, in another translation","body":"Verily, when there is no attachment, either to sense-objects, or to actions, having renounced all Sankalpas, then is one said to have attained concentration.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","4 of 47"]]},"gv-6-5":{"route":"#/gitav/6.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:5:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.5","text":"उद्धरेदात्मनाऽऽत्मानं नात्मानमवसादयेत् ।\nआत्मैव ह्यात्मनो बन्धुरात्मैव रिपुरात्मनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"uddharedātmanā’’tmānaṃ nātmānamavasādayet |\nātmaiva hyātmano bandhurātmaiva ripurātmanaḥ ||","body":"Let him raise the self by the Self and not let the self become depressed; for verily is the Self the friend of the self, and also the Self the self's enemy;","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","5 of 47"]]},"g2-6-5":{"route":"#/gitav/6.5","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:5:en2","title":"Gita 6.5, in another translation","body":"A man should uplift himself by his own self, so let him not weaken this self. For this self is the friend of oneself, and this self is the enemy of oneself.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","5 of 47"]]},"gv-6-6":{"route":"#/gitav/6.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:6:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.6","text":"बन्धुरात्माऽऽत्मनस्तस्य येनात्मैवात्मना जितः ।\nअनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत् ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"bandhurātmā’’tmanastasya yenātmaivātmanā jitaḥ |\nanātmanastu śatrutve vartetātmaiva śatruvat ||","body":"The Self is the friend of the self of him in whom the self by the Self is vanquished; but to the unsubdued self the Self verily becometh hostile as an enemy.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","6 of 47"]]},"g2-6-6":{"route":"#/gitav/6.6","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:6:en2","title":"Gita 6.6, in another translation","body":"The self (the active part of our nature) is the friend of the self, for him who has conquered himself by this self. But to the unconquered self, this self is inimical, (and behaves) like (an external) foe.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","6 of 47"]]},"gv-6-7":{"route":"#/gitav/6.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:7:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.7","text":"जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा समाहितः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु तथा मानापमानयोः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"jitātmanaḥ praśāntasya paramātmā samāhitaḥ |\nśītoṣṇasukhaduḥkheṣu tathā mānāpamānayoḥ ||","body":"The higher Self of him who is Self -controlled and peaceful is uniform in cold and heat, pleasure and pain, as well as in honour and dishonour.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","7 of 47"]]},"g2-6-7":{"route":"#/gitav/6.7","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:7:en2","title":"Gita 6.7, in another translation","body":"To the self-controlled and serene, the Supreme Self is, the object of constant, realisation, in cold and heat, pleasure and pain, as well as in honour and dishonour.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","7 of 47"]]},"gv-6-8":{"route":"#/gitav/6.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:8:en","title":"Bhagavad Gita 6.8","text":"ज्ञानविज्ञानतृप्तात्मा कूटस्थो विजितेन्द्रियः ।\nयुक्त इत्युच्यते योगी समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ॥","lang":"sa","roman":"jñānavijñānatṛptātmā kūṭastho vijitendriyaḥ |\nyukta ityucyate yogī samaloṣṭāśmakāñcanaḥ ||","body":"The Yogî who is satisfied with wisdom and knowledge, unwavering, whose senses are sub dued, to whom a lump of earth, a stone and gold are the same, is said to be harmonised.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","8 of 47"]]},"g2-6-8":{"route":"#/gitav/6.8","art":null,"source":"Sanskrit: the vulgate text of the IIT Kanpur Gita Supersite via gita/gita (public domain), checked against three other editions. English: Annie Besant (1922) and Swami Swarupananda (1909), both public domain.","cta":"Open this verse","why":"The Bhagavad Gita, chapter 6 — The Way of Meditation","src":"gita:6:8:en2","title":"Gita 6.8, in another translation","body":"Whose heart is filled with satisfaction by wisdom and realisation, and is changeless, whose senses are conquered, and to whom a lump of earth, stone, and gold are the same: that Yogi is called steadfast.","facts":[["Chapter","The Way of Meditation"],["Verse","8 of 47"]]}});
